nswer**\nThe product of 92 and 58 is \\boxed{5336}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 92 and 58, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. Multiply 92 by 8 (the ones place of 58):\n   \\[\n   92 \\times 8 = 736\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 92 by 50 (the tens place of 58, which is 5 shifted one position to the left):\n   \\[\n   92 \\times 50 = 4600\n   \\]\n3. Add the two partial products together:\n   \\[\n   736 + 4600 = 5336\n   \\]\n\nWe can verify this using the distributive property by breaking down the numbers:\n\\[\n92 \\times 58 = (90 + 2)(50 + 8)\n\\]\nExpanding this:\n\\[\n= 90 \\times 50 + 90 \\times 8 + 2 \\times 50 + 2 \\times 8\n\\]\n\\[\n= 4500 + 720 + 100 + 16\n\\]\nAdding these results:\n\\[\n4500 + 720 = 5220\n\\]\n\\[\n5220 + 100 = 5320\n\\]\n\\[\n5320 + 16 = 5336\n\\]\n\nAnother verification using the lattice method also confirms the result, and using the distributive property with subtraction:\n\\[\n92 \\times 58 = 92 \\times (60 - 2) = 92 \\times 60 - 92 \\times 2\n\\]\n\\[\n= 5520 - 184 = 5336\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 92 and 58 is \\boxed{5336}.",
