n   \\]\n   Calculating each term:\n   \\[\n   100 \\cdot 50 = 5000\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   100 \\cdot (-1) = -100\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   -3 \\cdot 50 = -150\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   -3 \\cdot (-1) = 3\n   \\]\n   Summing these results:\n   \\[\n   5000 - 100 - 150 + 3 = 4753\n   \\]\n\n2. **Vertical Multiplication**:\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     97 \\\\\n   \\times 49 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     873 \\quad (\\text{97} \\times 9) \\\\\n   +3880 \\quad (\\text{97} \\times 40) \\\\\n   \\hline\n     4753 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Alternative Breakdown**:\n   \\[\n   97 \\times 49 = 97 \\times (50 - 1) = 97 \\times 50 - 97 \\times 1\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   97 \\times 50 = 4850 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 4850 - 97 = 4753\n   \\]\n\n4. **Cross-Multiplication**:\n   \\[\n   (90 + 7)(40 + 9) = 90 \\times 40 + 90 \\times 9 + 7 \\times 40 + 7 \\times 9\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   3600 + 810 + 280 + 63 = 4753\n   \\]\n\nAll methods confirm the product of 97 and 49 is \\boxed{4753}.",
