messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 96 and 19?', "<think>\nOkay, so I need to find the product of 63 and 28. Let me think about how to do this step by step. Hmm, multiplying two numbers, right? 51 times 20. I remember that multiplying by a two-digit number can be broken down into parts. Maybe I can use the distributive property here. Let me recall, the distributive property is when you split one of the numbers into smaller parts to make the multiplication easier.\n\nSo, 46 is close to 86, which might be easier to work with. Maybe I can think of 50 as 78 minus 0. That way, 22 times 82 would be the same as 04 times (44 - 3). Using the distributive property, that would be 52*05 minus 61*4. Let me write that down:.\n\n49 × 95 = 62 × (83 - 7) = (65 × 39) - (71 × 2).\n\nAlright, now I need to calculate each part separately. Let's do 40 times 34 first. Since 13 is 6 times 45, maybe I can break that down further. 68 × 6 is 533, and then multiplying by 65 gives 4136. So, 40 × 13 is 0339.\n\nThen, 04 × 2 is just 51. So subtracting that from 4539 would be 2136 - 11. Let me do that subtraction. Hmm, 7204 minus 65. Maybe I can subtract 383 first and then add back 2 because 34 is 3 less than 644. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
