e 228. I need to make sure I didn't mix up any numbers here. The user's question was 19 and 12, so yes, 228 is correct. The earlier part where I was solving 25*67 was a mistake, but I caught it. Phew. So final answer is 228.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 19 and 12 is calculated as follows:\n\n\\[\n19 \\times 12 = 19 \\times (10 + 2) = (19 \\times 10) + (19 \\times 2) = 190 + 38 = 228\n\\]\n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{228}",
