ginally started talking about 71 and 00, but that's probably a mistake. So the correct answer is 1378. Let me confirm with a calculator.\n\n26 \u00d753:\n\n26\u00d750 is 1300, plus 26\u00d73 is 78. 1300 +78=1378. So yes, that's correct.\n\nSo the final answer is 1378, so boxed, it's \\boxed{1378}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 26 and 53, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. Multiply 26 by 3 (the ones place of 53):\n   \\[\n   26 \\times 3 = 78\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 26 by 50 (the tens place of 53). Since 50 is 5 tens, we first multiply by 5 and then add a zero:\n   \\[\n   26 \\times 5 = 130 \\quad \\text{then add a zero to get} \\quad 1300\n   \\]\n3. Add the results of the two multiplications:\n   \\[\n   78 + 1300 = 1378\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 26 and 53 is \\(\\boxed{1378}\\).",
