ding me to 8544, so that's probably the right answer.\n\nI think I confused myself at first when I was setting up the multiplication with different numbers, but after recalculating step by step, it's clear. So the product of 89 and 96 is 8544.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 89 and 96 is \\boxed{8544}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 89 and 96, we can use the standard multiplication method and verify using the distributive property.\n\nFirst, using the standard multiplication method:\n\n1. Multiply 96 by 9 (the units digit of 89):\n   \\[\n   96 \\times 9 = 864\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 96 by 80 (the tens digit of 89, which is 8 shifted one position to the left):\n   \\[\n   96 \\times 80 = 7680\n   \\]\n3. Add the results of the two multiplications:\n   \\[\n   864 + 7680 = 8544\n   \\]\n\nVerification using the distributive property:\n1. Break down 89 and 96:\n   \\[\n   89 \\times 96 = 89 \\times (90 + 6)\n   \\]\n2. Calculate each part separately:\n   \\[\n   89 \\times 90 = 8010\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   89 \\times 6 = 534\n   \\]\n3. Add the results:\n   \\[\n   8010 + 534 = 8544\n   \\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 89 and 96 is \\(\\boxed{8544}\\).",
