nAlternatively, breaking down 43 into 40 +3, so:\n\n(40 +3) \u00d7 92 = 40\u00d792 + 3\u00d792. .\n\n40\u00d792: 40\u00d790 = 3600, 40\u00d72=80 \u2192 total 3680. .\n\n3\u00d792 = 276. .\n\nAdding those: 3680 + 276 = 3956. .\n\nSame result. Hmm. So why did I get confused earlier? Because I started with different numbers. My initial process had a lot of errors, but upon redoing it correctly, it seems 3956 is the answer. .\n\nWait, but let me check with the standard multiplication algorithm again step by step. .\n\n\u2003\u200343  .\n\u00d7\u202f92  .\n--------\nFirst, multiply 43 by 2 (units place):\n\n2\u00d73=6, 2\u00d74=8 \u2192 86.\n\nThen multiply 43 by 9 (tens place, so actually 90). \n\n9\u00d73=27, write down 7 and carry over 2.\n\n9\u00d74=36 plus carryover 2 is 38. So that gives 387, but since it's the tens place, we shift left one, making it 3870.\n\nAdd 86 + 3870:\n\n3870.\n\n+\u202f\u00a086.\n\n= 3956.\n\nYes, that checks out. Therefore, the correct answer should be 3956. But wait, let me use another method to verify once more. .\n\nUsing the lattice method maybe. Or perhaps converting to addition. 43 added 92 times. But that would be tedious. Alternatively, using calculator math. But since I can't use a calculator, let's do another breakdown. .\n\nAlternatively, 92 \u00d7 43 can be thought of as (90 + 2)(40 +3). Using the FOIL method.\n\nFirst: 90\u00d740 = 3600.\n\nOuter: 90\u00d73 = 270.\n\nInner: 2\u00d740=80.\n\nLast: 2\u00d73=6.\n\nAdd all those together: 3600 +270 = 3870; 80 +6=86. Then 3870+86=3956. Same result. .\n\nTherefore, I think the correct product is 3956. But I want to make sure I didn't make a mistake in arithmetic anywhere. Let me re-add 3870 and 86. \n\n3870 + 80 is 3950, plus 6 is 3956. Yes. \n\nAlternatively, 43 \u00d7 92. Let me check with another approach. \n\n43 \u00d7 92 = 43 \u00d7 (100 - 8) = 43\u00d7100 - 43\u00d78 = 4300 - 344 = ?\n\n4300 - 344: 4300 - 300 is 4000, then subtract 44 more: 4000 -44 = 3956. \n\nYes, that works. So that confirms it again. \n\nHmm, so in my initial thinking process, I messed up the problem numbers, but after correcting myself, multiple methods give me 3956. So I think that's the right answer. Therefore, the product of 43 and 92 is 3956.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 43 and 92 is \\boxed{3956}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 43 and 92, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n   \\quad 43 \\\\\n\\times 92 \\\\\n\\hline\n   \\quad 86 \\quad (\\text{43 multiplied by 2}) \\\\\n+ 3870 \\quad (\\text{43 multiplied by 90}) \\\\\n\\hline\n   3956 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nBreaking it down step-by-step:\n1. Multiply 43 by 2 (the units digit of 92):\n   \\[\n   43 \\times 2 = 86\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 43 by 90 (the tens digit of 92, which is 9 in the tens place, so 90):\n   \\[\n   43 \\times 90 = 3870\n   \\]\n3. Add the two results together:\n   \\[\n   86 + 3870 = 3956\n   \\]\n\nVerification using the distributive property:\n\\[\n43 \\times 92 = 43 \\times (90 + 2) = 43 \\times 90 + 43 \\times 2 = 3870 + 86 = 3956\n\\]\n\nAnother verification using the FOIL method for \\((40 + 3)(90 + 2)\\):\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n&40 \\times 90 + 40 \\times 2 + 3 \\times 90 + 3 \\times 2 \\\\\n&= 3600 + 80 + 270 + 6 \\\\\n&= 3600 + 270 = 3870 \\\\\n&3870 + 80 = 3950 \\\\\n&3950 + 6 = 3956\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 43 and 92 is \\(\\boxed{3956}\\).",
