\n\n3. Multiply 48 by 9 (the tens place of 93, which is actually 90, so we shift one position to the left):\n   \\[\n   48 \\times 9 = 432 \\quad \\text{(then shift left by one, making it 4320)}\n   \\]\n\n4. Add the two partial products:\n   \\[\n   144 + 4320 = 4464\n   \\]\n\nVerification using the distributive property:\n\\[\n48 \\times 93 = (40 + 8)(90 + 3) = 40 \\times 90 + 40 \\times 3 + 8 \\times 90 + 8 \\times 3\n\\]\n\\[\n= 3600 + 120 + 720 + 24 = 3600 + 120 = 3720; \\quad 3720 + 720 = 4440; \\quad 4440 + 24 = 4464\n\\]\n\nAnother verification using alternative method:\n\\[\n48 \\times 93 = (50 - 2) \\times 93 = 50 \\times 93 - 2 \\times 93\n\\]\n\\[\n= 4650 - 186 = 4464\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 48 and 93 is \\boxed{4464}.",
