ybe I made a mistake in my initial wrong calculation because I started with the wrong numbers. But after redoing it properly, both methods give the same answer. So I feel confident now.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 67 and 54 is calculated as follows:\n\n**Step-by-Step Calculation:**\n\n1. **Break down the multiplication using the distributive property:**\n   \\[\n   67 \\times 54 = (60 + 7) \\times (50 + 4)\n   \\]\n\n2. **Expand the terms:**\n   \\[\n   = 60 \\times 50 + 60 \\times 4 + 7 \\times 50 + 7 \\times 4\n   \\]\n\n3. **Compute each part:**\n   - \\(60 \\times 50 = 3000\\)\n   - \\(60 \\times 4 = 240\\)\n   - \\(7 \\times 50 = 350\\)\n   - \\(7 \\times 4 = 28\\)\n\n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \\[\n   3000 + 240 = 3240 \\\\\n   3240 + 350 = 3590 \\\\\n   3590 + 28 = 3618\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**  \n\\boxed{3618}",
