andard multiplication method to verify.\n\nMultiplying 86 by 68:\n\nFirst, write it as:\n\n     86\n   x 68\n   ------\n\nMultiply 86 by 8 (units place of 68):\n\n86 x 8: 6x8=48, write down 8, carryover 4. 8x8=64 plus 4 is 68. So that's 688.\n\nThen multiply 86 by 60 (since the 6 in 68 is in the tens place, so it's 60):\n\n86 x 60: Well, 86 x6 = 516, then add a zero to get 5160.\n\nNow add the two results:\n\n688 + 5160 = 5848.\n\nSame result. So that seems correct.\n\nWait, but let me confirm once more because sometimes when I do mental math I might have errors. Let me do it another way.\n\nAlternatively, using the difference of squares or another method. Let me see.\n\nAlternatively, note that 86 \u00d7 68 can be written as (77 + 9)(77 - 9) but wait, 77 squared minus 9 squared? Wait, 77 is the average of 86 and 68?\n\nWait, 86 and 68. Let me check: (86 + 68)/2 = (154)/2 = 77. Yes! So, 86 = 77 + 9 and 68 = 77 - 9. Therefore, their product is 77\u00b2 - 9\u00b2.\n\nSo compute 77 squared minus 9 squared.\n\n77 squared: 70\u00b2 + 2\u00d770\u00d77 + 7\u00b2 = 4900 + 980 + 49 = 4900+980 is 5880, plus 49 is 5929.\n\n9 squared is 81. So 5929 - 81 = 5848. Same answer. Great, so that confirms it's 5848.\n\nTherefore, the product of 86 and 68 is 5848.\n\nWait, but let me check with another method just to be thorough. Let's use another distributive approach.\n\nAlternatively, 86 \u00d7 68 = 86 \u00d7 (70 - 2) = 86\u00d770 - 86\u00d72.\n\nCompute 86\u00d770: 86\u00d77 is 602, so 602 \u00d710=6020.\n\n86\u00d72=172.\n\nSubtracting: 6020 - 172 = 5848. Again, same result.\n\nHmm, so all methods are pointing to 5848. Therefore, that must be the correct answer. I think that's solid.\n\nInitially, I messed up by misreading the numbers, but after correcting myself and approaching it step by step, everything checks out. So the key was to apply different methods to confirm the result. It's easy to make a mistake with carrying over numbers or miscalculating partial products, so cross-verifying with alternative methods helps ensure accuracy.\n\nAnother way could be using the standard algorithm again but carefully:\n\n   86\nx 68\n-------\nFirst, 8\u00d76=48, write down 8, carryover 4.\n\nThen 8\u00d78=64 plus 4 is 68, so first partial product is 688.\n\nNext, multiply by the tens digit (6 in 68 is actually 60), so we shift one position:\n\n6\u00d76=36, write down 6, carryover 3.\n\n6\u00d78=48 plus 3 is 51, so that gives 5160 (since we shifted one place, it's 5160).\n\nAdding 688 + 5160:\n\n688 + 5160:\n\n688 + 5000 = 5688\n\n5688 + 160 = 5848. Yep, that's correct.\n\nAlright, so after multiple methods and checks, I'm confident that 86 multiplied by 68 equals 5848.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 86 and 68 is \\boxed{5848}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 86 and 68, we can use multiple methods to ensure accuracy.\n\n### Method 1: Distributive Property\nWe break down the numbers using the distributive property:\n\\[\n(80 + 6)(60 + 8) = 80 \\times 60 + 80 \\times 8 + 6 \\times 60 + 6 \\times 8\n\\]\nCalculating each term:\n\\[\n80 \\times 60 = 4800\n\\]\n\\[\n80 \\times 8 = 640\n\\]\n\\[\n6 \\times 60 = 360\n\\]\n\\[\n6 \\times 8 = 48\n\\]\nAdding these results together:\n\\[\n4800 + 640 + 360 + 48 = 5848\n\\]\n\n### Method 2: Standard Multiplication Algorithm\nMultiply 86 by 68 step-by-step:\n1. Multiply 86 by 8 (units place of 68):\n   \\[\n   86 \\times 8 = 688\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 86 by 60 (tens place of 68):\n   \\[\n   86 \\times 60 = 5160\n   \\]\n3. Add the partial products:\n   \\[\n   688 + 5160 = 5848\n   \\]\n\n### Method 3: Difference of Squares\nRecognize that 86 and 68 can be expressed as \\(77 + 9\\) and \\(77 - 9\\) respectively:\n\\[\n(77 + 9)(77 - 9) = 77^2 - 9^2\n\\]\nCalculating each term:\n\\[\n77^2 = 5929\n\\]\n\\[\n9^2 = 81\n\\]\nSubtracting these results:\n\\[\n5929 - 81 = 5848\n\\]\n\n### Method 4: Alternative Distributive Approach\nExpress 68 as \\(70 - 2\\):\n\\[\n86 \\times (70 - 2) = 86 \\times 70 - 86 \\times 2\n\\]\nCalculating each term:\n\\[\n86 \\times 70 = 6020\n\\]\n\\[\n86 \\times 2 = 172\n\\]\nSubtracting these results:\n\\[\n6020 - 172 = 5848\n\\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 86 and 68 is \\(\\boxed{5848}\\).",
