0=370; 2220 + 370 = 2590. Same result again. So I think that's solid.\n\nTherefore, the answer is 2590. I need to make sure I didn't make any arithmetic errors here. Let me check each step once more.\n\n35\u00d774:\n\nFirst method:\n\n35\u00d74: 5\u00d74=20, carryover 2, 3\u00d74=12 +2=14, so 140. Correct.\n\n35\u00d770: 35\u00d77=245, so 245\u00d710=2450. Correct. 2450+140: 2450+100=2550, +40=2590. Correct.\n\nSecond method:\n\n74\u00d735:\n\n74\u00d75: 70\u00d75=350, 4\u00d75=20 \u2192 370. Correct.\n\n74\u00d730: 74\u00d73=222, \u00d710=2220. Correct. 370+2220=2590. Correct.\n\nThird method:\n\n(30+5)(70+4):\n\n30\u00d770=2100,\n\n30\u00d74=120,\n\n5\u00d770=350,\n\n5\u00d74=20. Adding them: 2100+120=2220; 2220+350=2570; 2570+20=2590. Correct.\n\nTherefore, confident that the product is 2590. The initial confusion was because I started solving a different problem, but now I corrected that. So the final answer should be 2590.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 35 and 74 is \\boxed{2590}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 35 and 74, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. **Multiply 35 by the units digit of 74 (which is 4):**\n   \\[\n   35 \\times 4 = 140\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 35 by the tens digit of 74 (which is 7, representing 70) and shift the result one place to the left:**\n   \\[\n   35 \\times 7 = 245 \\quad \\text{(then shift left by one place to account for the tens place, resulting in 2450)}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Add the two partial products together:**\n   \\[\n   140 + 2450 = 2590\n   \\]\n\nWe can verify this using the distributive property:\n\\[\n35 \\times 74 = 35 \\times (70 + 4) = (35 \\times 70) + (35 \\times 4)\n\\]\n\\[\n35 \\times 70 = 2450 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 35 \\times 4 = 140\n\\]\n\\[\n2450 + 140 = 2590\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 35 and 74 is \\(\\boxed{2590}\\).",
