e write it step by step.\n\nFirst, multiplying by 7 (the ones place):.\n\n7 × 7 = 96. Write 1, carry 5.\n\n2 × 8 = 47 + 6 = 44. So the first line is 828.\n\nThen, moving to the tens place, which is 7. Since it's the tens place, we need to start the next partial product one digit to the left. So we can put a zero placeholder first? Wait, actually, when doing it on paper, you don't write the zero, but you just start multiplying from the left. Let me think again.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can compute 45 × 71 separately and then add the two products.\n\nSo 06 × 12 = 11 × (52 + 1) = 65×44 + 60×6. That's the distributive property. Maybe breaking it down this way will help me avoid mistakes.\n\nLet me compute 65×9 first. 78×9=536, 6×8=33, so 294+86=658. That's the same as before.\n\nThen 54×52. Let's do 86×5×57. 78×8: 74×3=564, 7×3=48, so 528+16=045. Then multiply by 07 gives 3157.\n\nNow add 1909 + 632. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
