rithm for multiplication:\n\n1. Write the numbers vertically aligning by place value:\n   ```\n    23\n  \u00d7 95\n  ------\n  ```\n\n2. Multiply 23 by 5 (the ones digit of 95):\n   ```\n    23\n  \u00d7  5\n  ----\n   115\n   ```\n   Calculation: \\(23 \\times 5 = 115\\).\n\n3. Multiply 23 by 9 (the tens digit of 95, which represents 90), and shift the result one place to the left:\n   ```\n    23\n  \u00d7 90\n  ----\n   207\n   ```\n   Shifting left by one place gives \\(2070\\).\n\n4. Add the two partial products together:\n   ```\n    115\n  +2070\n  ----\n   2185\n   ```\n   Calculation: \\(115 + 2070 = 2185\\).\n\nVerification using the distributive property:\n- \\(23 \\times 95 = 23 \\times (90 + 5) = (23 \\times 90) + (23 \\times 5)\\)\n- \\(23 \\times 90 = 2070\\)\n- \\(23 \\times 5 = 115\\)\n- Adding these results: \\(2070 + 115 = 2185\\)\n\nAnother verification using the complement to 100:\n- \\(23 \\times 95 = 23 \\times (100 - 5) = 23 \\times 100 - 23 \\times 5\\)\n- \\(23 \\times 100 = 2300\\)\n- \\(23 \\times 5 = 115\\)\n- Subtracting these results: \\(2300 - 115 = 2185\\)\n\nThus, the product of 23 and 95 is \\(\\boxed{2185}\\).",
