t the question is 30 and 98, so the answer should be 2940. I need to make sure I read the problem correctly next time. \n\nAlternatively, using the standard multiplication:\n\n   98\n\u00d7 30\n-----\n   00 (98 \u00d7 0)\n+2940 (98 \u00d7 30, shifted one position to the left)\n-----\n 2940\n\nYes, that's consistent. \n\nTherefore, the product of 30 and 98 is 2940.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 30 and 98 is calculated as follows:\n\n\\[\n30 \\times 98 = 30 \\times (100 - 2) = (30 \\times 100) - (30 \\times 2) = 3000 - 60 = 2940\n\\]\n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{2940}",
