. 8\u00d74 is 32 plus 2 is 34. So 348. Then times 10 is 3,480.\n\nNow add the two results: 609 + 3,480. \n\nAdding those together: 3,480 + 600 is 4,080, plus 9 is 4,089. \n\nWait, let me verify that again. 3,480 plus 609:\n\n3,480 + 600 = 4,080\n\n4,080 + 9 = 4,089. So the total is 4,089. \n\nAlternatively, using distributive property: \n\n87 \u00d7 47 = (80 + 7)(40 + 7). Expanding this:\n\n80\u00d740 + 80\u00d77 + 7\u00d740 + 7\u00d77.\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n80\u00d740 = 3,200\n\n80\u00d77 = 560\n\n7\u00d740 = 280\n\n7\u00d77 = 49\n\nAdding them up: 3,200 + 560 = 3,760; 3,760 + 280 = 4,040; 4,040 +49 = 4,089. \n\nSame result. \n\nAlternatively, maybe another method. Let me try breaking 47 into 50 - 3. \n\nSo 87 \u00d7 47 = 87 \u00d7 (50 - 3) = 87\u00d750 - 87\u00d73.\n\nCompute 87\u00d750: 87\u00d75 = 435, so 435\u00d710=4,350\n\nThen 87\u00d73 = 261\n\nSubtract: 4,350 - 261 = ?\n\n4,350 minus 200 is 4,150\n\n4,150 minus 61 is 4,089. \n\nSame answer again. So that must be correct. \n\nHmm, so my initial mistake was misreading the problem as 48\u00d782 instead of 87\u00d747, but now that I corrected that, the answer is 4,089. \n\nWait, let me confirm once more with another method, maybe vertically:\n\n     87\n   \u00d7 47\n   -----\n     609  (87\u00d77)\n   3480   (87\u00d740, shifted one position to the left)\n   -----\n    4089\n\nYes, adding those gives 4,089. \n\nTherefore, the correct product of 87 and 47 is 4,089.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 87 and 47 is \\boxed{4089}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 87 and 47, we can use the standard multiplication method:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n   \\hline\n   87 \\\\\n\\times 47 \\\\\n   \\hline\n   609 & \\text{(87 \u00d7 7)} \\\\\n+3480 & \\text{(87 \u00d7 40, shifted one position to the left)} \\\\\n   \\hline\n   4089 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nBreaking it down step-by-step:\n1. Multiply 87 by 7:\n   \\[\n   87 \\times 7 = 609\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 87 by 40 (which is 4 \u00d7 10):\n   \\[\n   87 \\times 40 = 3480\n   \\]\n3. Add the results of the two multiplications:\n   \\[\n   609 + 3480 = 4089\n   \\]\n\nVerification using the distributive property:\n\\[\n87 \\times 47 = (80 + 7)(40 + 7) = 80 \\times 40 + 80 \\times 7 + 7 \\times 40 + 7 \\times 7\n\\]\n\\[\n= 3200 + 560 + 280 + 49 = 3200 + 560 = 3760\n\\]\n\\[\n3760 + 280 = 4040\n\\]\n\\[\n4040 + 49 = 4089\n\\]\n\nAnother method using 47 as 50 - 3:\n\\[\n87 \\times 47 = 87 \\times (50 - 3) = 87 \\times 50 - 87 \\times 3\n\\]\n\\[\n87 \\times 50 = 4350 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 87 \\times 3 = 261\n\\]\n\\[\n4350 - 261 = 4089\n\\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 87 and 47 is \\(\\boxed{4089}\\).",
