5. Which matches the distributive method's result of 6,525.\n\nAh! So my first attempt had an error in the intermediate steps, probably miscalculating the partial products. So the correct answer is 6,525.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use another method, like multiplying 87 by 75 as (80 +7)(70 +5), but we already did that and got 6525. Alternatively, maybe using 75 as 75 = 70 +5, so 87\u00d775 =87*(70+5)=87\u00d770 +87\u00d75.\n\n87\u00d770: 87\u00d77\u00d710. 87\u00d77: 80\u00d77=560, 7\u00d77=49. So 560+49=609. Then times 10 is 6090.\n\n87\u00d75: 435 as before. So 6090+435=6525. Yep, same result.\n\nAlternatively, using 75 as 3/4 of 100, so 87 \u00d7 75 = 87 \u00d7 (3/4 \u00d7 100) = (87 \u00d7 3)/4 \u00d7100. Let's see:\n\n87 \u00d73 = 261. Then divide by 4: 261/4 =65.25, then multiply by 100 gives 6525. That works too. So that confirms it.\n\nSo the correct product is 6,525. My initial first method had a miscalculation, but after redoing it step by step, it's clear that 6525 is the right answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 87 and 75 is \\boxed{6525}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 87 and 75, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n   \\quad 87 \\\\\n\\times 75 \\\\\n\\hline\n   435 \\quad (\\text{87 multiplied by 5}) \\\\\n+6090 \\quad (\\text{87 multiplied by 70, shifted one position to the left}) \\\\\n\\hline\n   6525 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nBreaking it down step-by-step:\n1. Multiply 87 by 5:\n   \\[\n   87 \\times 5 = 435\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 87 by 70 (which is 7 in the tens place, so shifted one position left):\n   \\[\n   87 \\times 70 = 6090\n   \\]\n3. Add the results of the two multiplications:\n   \\[\n   435 + 6090 = 6525\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 87 and 75 is \\boxed{6525}.",
