sult.\n\nAlternatively, using another approach, perhaps 57\u00d772 = 57\u00d7(70+2) = 57\u00d770 + 57\u00d72, which is the same as before.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using the fact that 57\u00d772 = (60 - 3)\u00d772 = 60\u00d772 - 3\u00d772.\n\nCalculating:\n\n60\u00d772 = 4320\n\n3\u00d772 = 216\n\n4320 - 216 = 4104. Yep, same answer.\n\nTherefore, the product of 57 and 72 is 4104.\n\nWait, but in my first wrong problem with 98\u00d789, I had a different approach but messed up the numbers. But in any case, since I've verified with two methods here, I can be confident it's 4104. Let me just do a quick check with estimation to see if it makes sense.\n\n57 is close to 60, and 72 is close to 70. So 60\u00d770 = 4200. Our answer is 4104, which is a bit less, which makes sense because both numbers were rounded up. So that seems reasonable.\n\nAlternatively, another estimation: 57\u00d770 = 3990. Then adding 57\u00d72 more: 3990 + 114 = 4104. Yep, that's consistent.\n\nAlright, I think that's solid. So the answer is 4104.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 57 and 72 is \\boxed{4104}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 57 and 72, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n   \\quad 57 \\\\\n\\times 72 \\\\\n\\hline\n   114 \\quad (\\text{57 multiplied by 2}) \\\\\n+3990 \\quad (\\text{57 multiplied by 70, shifted one position to the left}) \\\\\n\\hline\n   4104 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nBreaking down the numbers using the distributive property:\n\\[\n57 \\times 72 = (50 + 7)(70 + 2)\n\\]\nExpanding the terms:\n\\[\n50 \\times 70 + 50 \\times 2 + 7 \\times 70 + 7 \\times 2\n\\]\nCalculating each term:\n\\[\n50 \\times 70 = 3500 \\\\\n50 \\times 2 = 100 \\\\\n7 \\times 70 = 490 \\\\\n7 \\times 2 = 14\n\\]\nAdding the results:\n\\[\n3500 + 100 + 490 + 14 = 4104\n\\]\n\nAnother verification using the difference of squares approach:\n\\[\n57 \\times 72 = (60 - 3) \\times 72 = 60 \\times 72 - 3 \\times 72\n\\]\nCalculating each term:\n\\[\n60 \\times 72 = 4320 \\\\\n3 \\times 72 = 216\n\\]\nSubtracting the results:\n\\[\n4320 - 216 = 4104\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 57 and 72 is \\boxed{4104}.",
