\n\n2. **Using standard long multiplication**:\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     100 \\\\\n   \\times 77 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     700 \\quad \\text{(100 \u00d7 7)} \\\\\n   +7000 \\quad \\text{(100 \u00d7 70, shifted one position to the left)} \\\\\n   \\hline\n     7700 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 100 and 77 is \\(\\boxed{7700}\\).",
