ore, the answer is 6205.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 73 and 85 is \\boxed{6205}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 73 and 85, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. **Multiply 73 by 5 (the ones place of 85):**\n   \\[\n   73 \\times 5 = 365\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: \\(70 \\times 5 = 350\\) and \\(3 \\times 5 = 15\\), so \\(350 + 15 = 365\\).\n\n2. **Multiply 73 by 80 (the tens place of 85, which is 8 \u00d7 10):**\n   \\[\n   73 \\times 80 = 5840\n   \\]\n   - First, calculate \\(73 \\times 8\\):\n     \\[\n     73 \\times 8 = 584\n     \\]\n     - Calculation: \\(70 \\times 8 = 560\\) and \\(3 \\times 8 = 24\\), so \\(560 + 24 = 584\\).\n   - Then multiply by 10:\n     \\[\n     584 \\times 10 = 5840\n     \\]\n\n3. **Add the two partial products:**\n   \\[\n   365 + 5840 = 6205\n   \\]\n\nUsing the distributive property for verification:\n\\[\n73 \\times 85 = (70 + 3)(80 + 5) = 70 \\times 80 + 70 \\times 5 + 3 \\times 80 + 3 \\times 5\n\\]\n- \\(70 \\times 80 = 5600\\)\n- \\(70 \\times 5 = 350\\)\n- \\(3 \\times 80 = 240\\)\n- \\(3 \\times 5 = 15\\)\n\nAdding these results:\n\\[\n5600 + 350 + 240 + 15 = 6205\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 73 and 85 is \\(\\boxed{6205}\\).",
