g distributive property another way: 60*92 = (6*10)*(9*10 + 2) = 6*9*10*10 +6*2*10 = 54*100 +12*10 = 5400 +120 =5520. \n\nAll methods lead to 5520, so that's correct. \n\nTherefore, I need to present the correct answer as 5520, after realizing that I initially confused the question with a different problem but then corrected myself through multiple verification methods. \n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 60 and 92 is \\boxed{5520}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 60 and 92, we can use the standard multiplication method:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n   92 \\\\\n\\times 60 \\\\\n\\hline\n   0 \\quad \\text{(92 multiplied by 0)} \\\\\n552 \\quad \\text{(92 multiplied by 6, shifted one position to the left)} \\\\\n\\hline\n5520 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nBreaking it down further, we can also compute it as:\n\\[\n60 \\times 92 = 60 \\times (90 + 2) = 60 \\times 90 + 60 \\times 2\n\\]\n\\[\n60 \\times 90 = 5400 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 60 \\times 2 = 120\n\\]\n\\[\n5400 + 120 = 5520\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 60 and 92 is \\boxed{5520}.",
