kenly thought the numbers were different, but after double-checking, it's clear. So the answer should be 520.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 26 and 20 is \\boxed{520}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 26 and 20, we can break down the multiplication into simpler steps. \n\nFirst, recognize that multiplying by 20 is the same as multiplying by 2 and then by 10. \n\n1. Multiply 26 by 2:\n   \\[\n   26 \\times 2 = 52\n   \\]\n\n2. Then multiply the result by 10:\n   \\[\n   52 \\times 10 = 520\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 26 and 20 is \\(\\boxed{520}\\).",
