d be 4324?\n\nLet me check using another method to confirm.\n\nAlternatively, using distributive property: (90 +2)(40+7) = 90\u00d740 + 90\u00d77 + 2\u00d740 +2\u00d77.\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n90\u00d740 = 3600\n\n90\u00d77 = 630\n\n2\u00d740 = 80\n\n2\u00d77 =14\n\nAdding them all together: 3600 + 630 = 4230; 4230 +80=4310; 4310 +14=4324. Yep, same result.\n\nAlternatively, I can use another check: 92\u00d747.\n\nLet me see, 92 \u00d750 would be 4600, but since it's 47, which is 50-3, so 92\u00d7(50-3)=92\u00d750 -92\u00d73=4600 -276= 4324. Correct.\n\nAlternatively, using calculator verification: 92\u00d747.\n\n92 \u00d747:\n\n92*40 = 3680, 92\u00d77=644. 3680+644=4324.\n\nYes, that's the same.\n\nSo the correct answer should be 4324. But in my initial incorrect steps, I messed up the numbers because I mixed up the problem's numbers. So I need to make sure I focus on the correct numbers given.\n\nTherefore, the product of 92 and 47 is 4324.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 92 and 47 is \\boxed{4324}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 92 and 47, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm and verify it with the distributive property.\n\nFirst, using the standard multiplication method:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n   \\quad 92 \\\\\n\\times 47 \\\\\n\\hline\n   644 \\quad (\\text{which is } 92 \\times 7) \\\\\n+3680 \\quad (\\text{which is } 92 \\times 40) \\\\\n\\hline\n   4324 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nBreaking it down step-by-step:\n1. Multiply 92 by 7:\n   \\[\n   92 \\times 7 = 644\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 92 by 40 (which is 92 \u00d7 4 \u00d7 10):\n   \\[\n   92 \\times 4 = 368 \\quad \\text{then} \\quad 368 \\times 10 = 3680\n   \\]\n3. Add the results of the two multiplications:\n   \\[\n   644 + 3680 = 4324\n   \\]\n\nUsing the distributive property:\n\\[\n(90 + 2)(40 + 7) = 90 \\times 40 + 90 \\times 7 + 2 \\times 40 + 2 \\times 7\n\\]\nCalculating each term:\n\\[\n90 \\times 40 = 3600 \\\\\n90 \\times 7 = 630 \\\\\n2 \\times 40 = 80 \\\\\n2 \\times 7 = 14\n\\]\nAdding them together:\n\\[\n3600 + 630 + 80 + 14 = 4324\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 92 and 47 is \\(\\boxed{4324}\\).",
