pose any numbers. 3 times 34 is 102, 70 times 34 is 2380, sum is 2482. Correct. Okay, so the product is 2482.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 34 and 73 is \\boxed{2482}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 34 and 73, we can use the standard algorithm and the distributive property for verification.\n\nFirst, using the standard algorithm:\n\n1. Multiply 34 by the units digit of 73 (which is 3):\n   \\[\n   34 \\times 3 = 102\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 34 by the tens digit of 73 (which is 7, representing 70), and shift the result one position to the left:\n   \\[\n   34 \\times 70 = 2380\n   \\]\n3. Add the two partial products:\n   \\[\n   102 + 2380 = 2482\n   \\]\n\nUsing the distributive property for verification:\n\\[\n(30 + 4) \\times (70 + 3) = 30 \\times 70 + 30 \\times 3 + 4 \\times 70 + 4 \\times 3\n\\]\nCalculating each term:\n\\[\n30 \\times 70 = 2100\n\\]\n\\[\n30 \\times 3 = 90\n\\]\n\\[\n4 \\times 70 = 280\n\\]\n\\[\n4 \\times 3 = 12\n\\]\nAdding these together:\n\\[\n2100 + 90 + 280 + 12 = 2482\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 34 and 73 is \\(\\boxed{2482}\\).",
