34, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. Multiply 97 by 4 (the ones place of 34):\n   \\[\n   97 \\times 4 = 388\n   \\]\n   - Calculation steps:\n     - \\(7 \\times 4 = 28\\) (write down 8, carry over 2)\n     - \\(9 \\times 4 = 36 + 2 = 38\\)\n\n2. Multiply 97 by 30 (the tens place of 34, which is 3 in the tens place, so 30):\n   \\[\n   97 \\times 30 = 2910\n   \\]\n   - Calculation steps:\n     - First calculate \\(97 \\times 3 = 291\\)\n     - Then add a zero to account for the tens place: \\(291 \\times 10 = 2910\\)\n\n3. Add the two results together:\n   \\[\n   388 + 2910 = 3298\n   \\]\n   - Verification steps:\n     - \\(388 + 2910\\) can be broken down as \\(388 + 2000 = 2388\\), then \\(2388 + 910 = 3298\\)\n\nUsing the distributive property for verification:\n\\[\n(100 - 3) \\times (30 + 4) = 100 \\times 30 + 100 \\times 4 - 3 \\times 30 - 3 \\times 4\n\\]\n\\[\n= 3000 + 400 - 90 - 12 = 3400 - 90 - 12 = 3310 - 12 = 3298\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 97 and 34 is \\(\\boxed{3298}\\).",
