\\\\\n   \\times 44 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     164 \\quad (\\text{41 multiplied by 4}) \\\\\n   + 1640 \\quad (\\text{41 multiplied by 40, shifted one position to the left}) \\\\\n   \\hline\n     1804 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Verification using distributive property:**\n   \\[\n   41 \\times 44 = 41 \\times (40 + 4) = (41 \\times 40) + (41 \\times 4)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   41 \\times 40 = 1640\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   41 \\times 4 = 164\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   1640 + 164 = 1804\n   \\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 41 and 44 is \\(\\boxed{1804}\\).",
