s 558.\n\nThen, multiply 62 by 40 (the tens place of 49, so it's 4 followed by a zero, so 40). So 62 \u00d7 40.\n\nFirst compute 62 \u00d7 4 = 248, then add a zero to get 2480.\n\nNow add the two results: 558 + 2480. Let's see:\n\n558 + 2480. Adding units: 8 + 0 = 8, tens: 5 + 8 = 13, hundreds: 5 + 4 = 9 plus the 1 carried over is 10, and thousands: 2 + 0 = 2 plus the carried over 1 is 3. Wait, that doesn't seem right. Wait, let me do it step by step.\n\nWait, actually:\n\n558 + 2480:\n\nAligning the numbers:\n\n  558\n\n+2480\n\n= ?\n\nStart from the right:\n\n8 + 0 = 8.\n\n5 + 8 = 13, write 3, carryover 1.\n\n5 + 4 = 9, plus the carried 1 is 10, so write 0 and carryover 1.\n\nFinally, the thousands place: 2 (from 2480) plus the carried over 1 is 3.\n\nSo total is 3038? Wait, but 558 + 2480: 558 + 2000 is 2558, plus 480 is 2558 + 480 = 3038. Yes, that's right.\n\nWait, but 62 \u00d7 49 = 3038?\n\nWait, let me check with another method to verify.\n\nAlternatively, using the distributive property:\n\n62 \u00d7 49 can be considered as 62 \u00d7 (50 - 1) = 62\u00d750 - 62\u00d71.\n\n62\u00d750: 62\u00d75 is 310, so times 10 is 3100.\n\nMinus 62 gives 3100 - 62 = 3038. So that matches.\n\nAlternatively, using another breakdown: 49 is 7\u00d77, so 62\u00d77\u00d77. 62\u00d77 is 434, then 434\u00d77. Let's see: 434\u00d77. 400\u00d77=2800, 34\u00d77=238. So 2800+238=3038. Yep, same result.\n\nOkay, so that seems correct. But let me verify with standard multiplication again, just to be sure.\n\n62 \u00d7 49:\n\nFirst line (times 9):\n\n62 \u00d7 9:\n\n2\u00d79=18, write 8, carryover 1. 6\u00d79=54 +1=55. So 558.\n\nSecond line (times 40, so shifted one position left):\n\n62 \u00d74 = 248, then add a zero: 2480.\n\nAdding them: 558 + 2480.\n\nYes, 558 + 2000 is 2558, plus 480 is 3038. Correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can do 49 \u00d7 60 + 49 \u00d7 2.\n\n49\u00d760: 49\u00d76=294, so 2940.\n\n49\u00d72=98.\n\n2940 +98 = 3038. Yep.\n\nTherefore, the product of 62 and 49 is