 the bottom number, which is 9.\n\nMultiply 9 \u00d7 58:\n\n9 \u00d7 8 = 72. Write down 2, carry over 7.\n\n9 \u00d7 5 = 45, plus 7 is 52. So the first partial product is 522.\n\nNow, moving to the tens digit of the bottom number, which is 7 (in the tens place, so it's 70).\n\nMultiply 70 \u00d7 58. Since it's the tens place, we shift one position to the left (i.e., multiply by 7 and then add a zero).\n\nFirst, multiply 7 \u00d7 8 = 56. Write down 6, carry over 5.\n\n7 \u00d7 5 = 35, plus 5 is 40. So the multiplication gives 406, and then adding the zero gives 4060.\n\nNow, add the two partial products:\n\n522\n\n+4060\n\n------\n\nAdding these together: 522 + 4060 = 4582.\n\nWait, but let me verify this another way to be sure. Let's try breaking it down using distributive property.\n\n58 \u00d7 79 can be written as (50 + 8) \u00d7 (70 + 9).\n\nExpanding this:\n\n50\u00d770 + 50\u00d79 + 8\u00d770 + 8\u00d79\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n50\u00d770 = 3500\n\n50\u00d79 = 450\n\n8\u00d770 = 560\n\n8\u00d79 = 72\n\nNow add them all together:\n\n3500 + 450 = 3950\n\n3950 + 560 = 4510\n\n4510 + 72 = 4582\n\nOkay, so that matches the previous result of 4582. Therefore, the product of 58 and 79 is 4582.\n\nWait, but let me try another method to be absolutely sure. Maybe vertical multiplication again, perhaps I made a mistake the first time.\n\nWait, let me try multiplying 58 by 79 vertically again:\n\nFirst, 58 \u00d7 9:\n\n9 \u00d7 8 = 72, write 2, carry 7.\n\n9 \u00d7 5 = 45 +7 = 52. So 522.\n\nThen, 58 \u00d7 70 (since the 7 is in the tens place):\n\n58 \u00d7 7 = ?\n\n5 \u00d77 = 35, 8\u00d77=56. So 58\u00d77:\n\n7\u00d78=56, write 6, carry 5.\n\n7\u00d75=35 +5=40. So 406. Then times 10 is 4060.\n\nAdding 522 + 4060:\n\n522 + 4000 = 4522, plus 60 more is 4582. Yep, same result.\n\nAlternatively, using the commutative property, multiplying 79 \u00d758.\n\nLet's do that as a check.\n\n79 \u00d758:\n\nFirst, 79 \u00d78 = 632\n\nThen 79 \u00d750 = 3950.\n\nAdd them together