otal is 3200 + 160 = 3360. Yep, same result. \n\nOr, using the commutative property, 42*80 is the same as 80*42, so maybe calculate 42*80. 42*8 is 336, so 42*80 is 3360. \n\nAll methods point to 3360. I think my initial confusion was because I was working with different numbers in my head, but now I've clarified it. So the product of 80 and 42 is 3360. I should write that as the final answer.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 80 and 42 is calculated by multiplying the two numbers together:\n\n\\[\n80 \\times 42 = 3360\n\\]\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n1. **Breakdown using distributive property:**\n   \\[\n   80 \\times 42 = 80 \\times (40 + 2) = (80 \\times 40) + (80 \\times 2)\n   \\]\n   - \\(80 \\times 40 = 3200\\)\n   - \\(80 \\times 2 = 160\\)\n   - Add the results: \\(3200 + 160 = 3360\\)\n\n2. **Alternative method (direct multiplication):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     \\quad 80 \\\\\n   \\times 42 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     160 \\quad (\\text{80 \u00d7 2}) \\\\\n   +3200 \\quad (\\text{80 \u00d7 40, shifted left}) \\\\\n   \\hline\n     3360 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:** \\(\\boxed{3360}\\)",
