perty.\n\n83 \u00d7 58 can be broken into (80 + 3) \u00d7 (50 + 8).\n\nUsing (a + b)(c + d) = ac + ad + bc + bd:\n\n80\u00d750 + 80\u00d78 + 3\u00d750 + 3\u00d78.\n\nCompute each term:\n\n80\u00d750 = 4000\n\n80\u00d78 = 640\n\n3\u00d750 = 150\n\n3\u00d78 = 24\n\nAdding them all together:\n\n4000 + 640 = 4640\n\n4640 + 150 = 4790\n\n4790 + 24 = 4814. Same result.\n\nSo the correct answer should be 4814. In my first mistaken approach, I was using different numbers (37 and 63), which led to confusion, but after correcting, it's clear the answer is 4814.\n\nAlternatively, to double-check with another method, maybe using the difference of squares or another property? Let's see.\n\nAlternatively, 83 \u00d7 58 can be thought of as (80 + 3)(60 - 2). Wait, but 58 is 60-2. Let me try that.\n\nSo (80 + 3)(60 - 2) = 80\u00d760 + 80\u00d7(-2) + 3\u00d760 + 3\u00d7(-2)\n\nWhich is 4800 - 160 + 180 - 6\n\nCalculating step by step:\n\n4800 - 160 = 4640\n\n4640 + 180 = 4820\n\n4820 - 6 = 4814. Same result again. Okay, that confirms it.\n\nAlternatively, using calculator verification: 83 multiplied by 58.\n\nWell, 80\u00d760 is 4800, but we have 83\u00d758. 80\u00d758 is 4640, plus 3\u00d758=174, so 4640+174=4814. Yep.\n\nTherefore, the product is 4814. I think that's solid. The initial confusion was because I misread the numbers and started with different values, but upon correcting and using multiple methods, it's clear the answer is 4814.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 83 and 58 is \\boxed{4814}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 83 and 58, we can use the distributive property by breaking down the numbers into smaller parts:\n\n\\[\n83 \\times 58 = (80 + 3) \\times (50 + 8)\n\\]\n\nApplying the distributive property \\((a + b)(c + d) = ac + ad + bc + bd\\):\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n80 \\times 50 & = 4000, \\\\\n80 \\times 8 & = 640, \\\\\n3 \\times 50 & = 150, \\\\\n3 \\times 8 & = 24.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nAdding these results together:\n\n\\[\n4000 + 640 + 150 + 24 = 48