\n(90 - 2) \u00d7 95 = 90\u00d795 - 2\u00d795.\n\nCalculating 90\u00d795: 90\u00d795 = 90\u00d7(90 +5) = 90\u00d790 + 90\u00d75 = 8100 + 450 = 8550.\n\nThen subtract 2\u00d795 = 190. So 8550 - 190 = 8360. Same answer.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps using 88 \u00d7 95 = 88 \u00d7 (100 - 5) = 88\u00d7100 - 88\u00d75 = 8800 - 440 = 8360. There we go, that's another way and it confirms the same result.\n\nOkay, so I think the correct answer is 8360. The first time I messed up the breakdown by possibly miscalculating the terms or breaking the numbers incorrectly, but upon using different methods like standard multiplication, distributive property correctly applied, and the distributive method with subtraction, I arrived at the same answer each time. So I feel confident that 88 multiplied by 95 is indeed 8360.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 88 and 95 is \\boxed{8360}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 88 and 95, we can use the distributive property and verify using different methods.\n\nFirst, we break down the numbers using the distributive property:\n\\[\n(80 + 8)(90 + 5)\n\\]\nExpanding this, we get:\n\\[\n80 \\times 90 + 80 \\times 5 + 8 \\times 90 + 8 \\times 5\n\\]\n\nCalculating each term separately:\n\\[\n80 \\times 90 = 7200\n\\]\n\\[\n80 \\times 5 = 400\n\\]\n\\[\n8 \\times 90 = 720\n\\]\n\\[\n8 \\times 5 = 40\n\\]\n\nAdding these results together:\n\\[\n7200 + 400 + 720 + 40 = 7200 + 400 = 7600\n\\]\n\\[\n7600 + 720 = 8320\n\\]\n\\[\n8320 + 40 = 8360\n\\]\n\nWe can also verify using another method by expressing 95 as \\(100 - 5\\):\n\\[\n88 \\times 95 = 88 \\times (100 - 5) = 88 \\times 100 - 88 \\times 5\n\\]\nCalculating each term:\n\\[\n88 \\times 100 = 8800\n\\]\n\\[\n88 \\times 5 = 440\n\\]\n\nSubtracting these results:\n\\[\n8800 - 440 = 8360\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 88 and 95 is \\(\\boxed{8360}\\).",
