rst steps when I thought it was 75 and 65. That was confusing myself. Let me correct.\n\nLet me start fresh. \n\nQuestion: What is the product of 37 and 44?\n\nAlright, so 37 \u00d7 44.\n\nLet me do the standard multiplication:\n\n   37  \n\u00d7 44  \n------  \nFirst multiply 37 by 4 (the units digit of 44):\n\n37 \u00d7 4 = 148.\n\nThen multiply 37 by 40 (the tens digit of 44):\n\n37 \u00d7 40 = 1480.\n\nAdd the two results together:\n\n148 + 1480 = 1628.\n\nTherefore, the product is 1628.\n\nAlternatively, to check, I can use another method like the distributive property:\n\n37 \u00d7 44 = (30 + 7) \u00d7 (40 + 4)\n\nExpand this:\n\n30\u00d740 + 30\u00d74 + 7\u00d740 + 7\u00d74\n\n= 1200 + 120 + 280 + 28\n\nAdding these:\n\n1200 + 120 = 1320\n\n1320 + 280 = 1600\n\n1600 + 28 = 1628.\n\nSame result. That's reassuring.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using the difference of squares or another trick? Let's see.\n\nAlternatively, 37 \u00d7 44 can be thought of as 37 \u00d7 (40 + 4), which is what we did earlier. \n\nAlternatively, if I think in terms of 37 \u00d7 44 = 37 \u00d7 (4 \u00d7 11) = (37 \u00d7 4) \u00d7 11. \n\n37 \u00d7 4 is 148, then 148 \u00d7 11. \n\nMultiplying by 11: 148 \u00d7 10 = 1480, plus 148 = 1480 + 148 = 1628. \n\nSame result again.\n\nOkay, so all methods lead to 1628. So the answer should be 1628. \n\nWait, maybe I can verify using a calculator? Since I don't have a calculator, but let me do it step by step again.\n\n37 \u00d7 44:\n\nFirst, 37 \u00d7 44. Let me write it vertically:\n\n      37  \n    \u00d744  \n    -----  \n      148  (this is 37 \u00d7 4)  \n    +1480  (this is 37 \u00d7 40, shifted one position to the left)  \n    -------  \n      1628  \n\nYes, adding 148 and 1480 gives 1628. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 1628.\n\nI think my confusion earlier was because I initially thought the numbers were different (maybe I misread 75 and 65, but the user's question is 37 and 44). So after correcting that, all methods confirm the result. So I'm confident the answer is 1628.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 37 and 44 is \\boxed{1628}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 37 and 44, we can use the standard multiplication method:\n\n1. Multiply 37 by 4 (the units digit of 44):\n   \\[\n   37 \\times 4 = 148\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 37 by 40 (the tens digit of 44):\n   \\[\n   37 \\times 40 = 1480\n   \\]\n\n3. Add the results of the two multiplications:\n   \\[\n   148 + 1480 = 1628\n   \\]\n\nWe can verify this using the distributive property:\n\\[\n37 \\times 44 = (30 + 7) \\times (40 + 4)\n\\]\nExpanding this:\n\\[\n30 \\times 40 + 30 \\times 4 + 7 \\times 40 + 7 \\times 4\n\\]\nCalculating each term:\n\\[\n1200 + 120 + 280 + 28 = 1200 + 120 = 1320\n\\]\n\\[\n1320 + 280 = 1600\n\\]\n\\[\n1600 + 28 = 1628\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 37 and 44 is \\(\\boxed{1628}\\).",
