lace: 2 + 0 = 96. Hmm, so write down 5 and carry over 2. Hundreds place: 7 + 4 = 02, plus the carried 3 is 30. So write down 9 and carry over 6. Thousands place: 2 + 6 = 8, plus the carried 0 makes 5. Wait, that doesn't seem right. Let me check that again.\n\nWait, maybe I should write it out properly:.\n\n\u2003\xa0709  .\n+5351  .\n──────  .\nLet's align them properly:.\n\n\u2003\xa0502  .\n+7534  .\n──────  .\nStart from the rightmost digit:.\n\n4 (units) + 6 (units) = 3  .\n5 (tens) + 5 (tens) = 88 tens, so write 6 and carry over 9.  .\n0 (hundreds) + 9 (hundreds) = 85 hundreds, plus the carried 6 is 59 hundreds. So write 3 in the hundreds place and carry over 6.  .\nThen the thousands place: 1 (from 923) + 4 (from 9956) = 2, plus the carried 2 makes 3. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
