3 in tens place is 30). So write a zero first:\n\n2\u00d73 = 6, write down 6.\n\n5\u00d73 = 15. So that gives 1560.\n\nAdd 416 and 1560 together:\n\n416 + 1560 = 1976.\n\nWait, let me check that addition again. 416 + 1560:\n\n400 + 1500 = 1900,\n\n16 + 60 = 76,\n\nSo total is 1976. That seems right.\n\nAlternatively, using distributive property:\n\n52 \u00d7 38 = (50 + 2)(30 + 8).\n\nExpanding:\n\n50\u00d730 + 50\u00d78 + 2\u00d730 + 2\u00d78.\n\nCalculate each term:\n\n50\u00d730 = 1500,\n\n50\u00d78 = 400,\n\n2\u00d730 = 60,\n\n2\u00d78 = 16.\n\nAdding those together: 1500 + 400 = 1900,\n\n1900 + 60 = 1960,\n\n1960 + 16 = 1976.\n\nSame result. So that's consistent.\n\nAlternatively, another method: using (a+b)(a-b) but not sure if that applies here. Alternatively, maybe think of 52 \u00d7 40 = 2080, then subtract 52 \u00d7 2 = 104, so 2080 - 104 = 1976. Yeah that works too.\n\nSo all methods give me 1976. Let me just confirm with calculator steps:\n\n52 multiplied by 38:\n\n52 \u00d7 30 = 1560,\n\n52 \u00d7 8 = 416,\n\nAdding them gives 1560 + 416 = 1976. Yep, that's correct.\n\nTherefore, the product of 52 and 38 is 1976.\n\nBut wait, just to be absolutely sure, let me do the multiplication step by step again:\n\n52 \u00d7 38.\n\nFirst, 52 \u00d7 8:\n\n2 \u00d7 8 = 16,\n\n5 \u00d7 8 = 40, plus the 1 carried over is 41. So that's 416.\n\nThen 52 \u00d7 30:\n\n52 \u00d7 3 = 156, so times 10 is 1560.\n\nAdding 416 + 1560:\n\n416 + 1500 = 1916,\n\n1916 + 60 = 1976. Correct.\n\nAlright, so after multiple checks, I'm confident the answer is 1976.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 52 and 38 is \\boxed{1976}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 52 and 38, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm and verify with the distributive property.\n\nFirst, using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n   52 \\\\\n\\times 38 \\\\\n\\hline\n   416 \\quad (\\text{52 multiplied by 8}) \\\\\n+1560 \\quad (\\text{52 multiplied by 30, shifted one position to the left}) \\\\\n\\hline\n  1976 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nBreaking down the multiplication:\n- \\(52 \\times 8 = 416\\)\n- \\(52 \\times 30 = 1560\\)\n\nAdding the results:\n\\[\n416 + 1560 = 1976\n\\]\n\nUsing the distributive property:\n\\[\n52 \\times 38 = (50 + 2)(30 + 8)\n\\]\nExpanding the terms:\n\\[\n50 \\times 30 + 50 \\times 8 + 2 \\times 30 + 2 \\times 8\n\\]\nCalculating each term:\n\\[\n50 \\times 30 = 1500, \\quad 50 \\times 8 = 400, \\quad 2 \\times 30 = 60, \\quad 2 \\times 8 = 16\n\\]\nAdding these together:\n\\[\n1500 + 400 + 60 + 16 = 1976\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 52 and 38 is \\(\\boxed{1976}\\).",
