s. Let me clarify:\n\nMultiplying by the units digit (8) gives 712.\n\nMultiplying by the tens digit (8) but since it's the tens place, it's actually 80 \u00d7 89. So:\n\n80 \u00d7 89:\n\nFirst compute 8 \u00d7 89 = 712, then add a zero to make it 7120.\n\nWait, but actually, when you do it step by step:\n\n8 (tens place) \u00d7 9 = 72. Wait no, this is getting confusing. Let me use the standard algorithm again properly.\n\nLet me write it out vertically:\n\n     89\n\n   \u00d7 88\n\n   -------\n\nFirst line: 89 \u00d7 8 (units place):\n\n9\u00d78=72, write 2, carryover 7.\n\n8\u00d78=64 +7=71. So first partial product is 712.\n\nSecond line: 89 \u00d7 8 (the tens place, so actually 80). So we shift one position to the left.\n\nNow compute 8 (from the tens digit) \u00d7 89:\n\n9\u00d78=72, write down 2, carryover 7.\n\n8\u00d78=64 +7=71. So that gives 712 again, but shifted left by one digit, so it becomes 7120.\n\nNow add the two partial products:\n\n712 + 7120 = 7832.\n\nSo that matches the second method. So the correct answer is 7832.\n\nWait, so where did I go wrong in my first calculation? Let me check again. Initially, I thought the numbers were 73 and 62 but then realized it was 89 and 88. So my second method with the distributive property was correct. The first partial product was actually when I was confused with the wrong numbers, so the 10201 was incorrect.\n\nAlternatively, another way to compute 89\u00d788 is using the identity (a)(a - 1) = a\u00b2 - a. Since 89 and 88 are consecutive numbers, but here it's 89\u00d788, which is n(n-1) where n=89. Therefore, 89 squared minus 89.\n\nCalculating 89 squared: 89\u00d789. Let me compute that first.\n\n89 squared:\n\n(90 -1)^2 = 90\u00b2 - 2\u00d790\u00d71 +1\u00b2 = 8100 - 180 +1 = 8100-180 is 7920, plus 1 is 7921.\n\nTherefore, 89 squared is 7921. Subtract 89: 7921 -89 = 7832. Yep, same result.\n\nAlternatively, another method: 88\u00d790 = (88\u00d79)\u00d710. Wait, no. Alternatively, 88\u00d790 is 88\u00d