. Let me confirm once more with another method.\n\nAlternatively, 94 \u00d7 47 can be calculated as (95 -1) \u00d7 47. 95\u00d747 is (100-5)\u00d747 = 100\u00d747 -5\u00d747 = 4700 - 235 = 4465. Then subtract 1\u00d747=47, so 4465-47=4418. Yep, that works too.\n\nTherefore, the product of 94 and 47 is 4,418. I think that's correct now. My initial confusion was because I started with a different problem but caught myself and corrected it. So the final answer is 4418.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 94 and 47 is calculated as follows:\n\n**Step-by-Step Calculation:**\n\n1. **Break down the numbers using the distributive property:**\n   \\[\n   94 \\times 47 = (90 + 4) \\times (40 + 7)\n   \\]\n   \n2. **Expand the multiplication:**\n   \\[\n   = 90 \\times 40 + 90 \\times 7 + 4 \\times 40 + 4 \\times 7\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate each term:**\n   - \\( 90 \\times 40 = 3,\\!600 \\)\n   - \\( 90 \\times 7 = 630 \\)\n   - \\( 4 \\times 40 = 160 \\)\n   - \\( 4 \\times 7 = 28 \\)\n\n4. **Sum the results:**\n   \\[\n   3,\\!600 + 630 = 4,\\!230 \\\\\n   4,\\!230 + 160 = 4,\\!390 \\\\\n   4,\\!390 + 28 = 4,\\!418\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**  \nThe product of 94 and 47 is **4,418**.  \n\n\\boxed{4418}",
