od to be sure.\n\nAnother way could be using the distributive property. Let's express 84 as (80 +4). Thus:\n\n85 \u00d7 (80 +4) = 85\u00d780 +85\u00d74.\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n85\u00d780: 85\u00d78\u00d710. 85\u00d78 is 680, so 680\u00d710=6800.\n\n85\u00d74 is 340.\n\nAgain, 6800 +340=7140. Same result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using the difference of squares or another algebraic identity? Let's see.\n\nHmm, 85\u00d784 can be thought of as (80+5)(80-1 +4)... Not sure if that's helpful. Alternatively, perhaps express them as numbers around 80 or another base.\n\nAlternatively, notice that 85\u00d784 is (80+5)(80+4). Let me expand this:\n\n(80 +5)(80 +4) = 80\u00d780 +80\u00d74 +5\u00d780 +5\u00d74.\n\nCalculate each term:\n\n80\u00d780 = 6400,\n\n80\u00d74 = 320,\n\n5\u00d780 = 400,\n\n5\u00d74 =20.\n\nAdding all together: 6400 +320 =6720; 6720 +400 =7120; 7120 +20=7140. Same answer again.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using the identity (a)(a-1) where a is 85? Wait, no, because 84 is 85-1, so 85\u00d784 =85\u00d7(85-1) =85\u00b2 -85.\n\nCalculating 85 squared: 85\u00b2 is (80+5)^2 =80\u00b2 +2\u00d780\u00d75 +5\u00b2 =6400 +800 +25 =7225.\n\nThen subtract 85: 7225 -85 =7225 -80 -5 =7145 -5 =7140. There we go. That also gives 7140.\n\nSo all methods are pointing to 7140. Therefore, the product of 85 and 84 is 7140.\n\nWait, but let me just do the straight multiplication once more to be absolutely sure.\n\nMultiplying 85 by 84:\n\n   85  \n\u00d7 84  \n-------  \nFirst, multiply 85 by 4: 85*4=340.\n\nThen multiply 85 by 80: 85*80=6800.\n\nAdding 340+6800: 340+6800.\n\n340 + 6800: 6800 + 300 =7100, plus 40 is 7140. Correct.\n\nAlternatively, if I do 84\u00d780=6720, then 84\u00d75=420, so 6720 +420=7140. Yes, same result.\n\nTherefore, I can confidently say the product of 85 and 84 is 7140.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 85 and 84 is \\boxed{7140}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 85 and 84, we can use the standard multiplication method:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n   85 \\\\\n\\times 84 \\\\\n\\hline\n   340 \\quad (\\text{85 multiplied by 4}) \\\\\n+6800 \\quad (\\text{85 multiplied by 80}) \\\\\n\\hline\n  7140 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nBreaking it down step-by-step:\n1. Multiply 85 by 4: \\(85 \\times 4 = 340\\).\n2. Multiply 85 by 80: \\(85 \\times 80 = 6800\\).\n3. Add the results of the two multiplications: \\(340 + 6800 = 7140\\).\n\nWe can also verify this using the distributive property:\n\\[\n85 \\times 84 = 85 \\times (80 + 4) = (85 \\times 80) + (85 \\times 4) = 6800 + 340 = 7140\n\\]\n\nAnother method using algebraic identity:\n\\[\n85 \\times 84 = 85 \\times (85 - 1) = 85^2 - 85\n\\]\nCalculating \\(85^2\\):\n\\[\n85^2 = (80 + 5)^2 = 80^2 + 2 \\times 80 \\times 5 + 5^2 = 6400 + 800 + 25 = 7225\n\\]\nSubtracting 85:\n\\[\n7225 - 85 = 7225 - 80 - 5 = 7140\n\\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 85 and 84 is \\(\\boxed{7140}\\).",
