eems correct. Maybe I was overcomplicating earlier, but both methods give me 6231. So I think that's the right answer. Let me just check with another approach, perhaps using rounding. \n\n67 \u00d7 93. If I round 93 to 90, then 67\u00d790 = 6030. But since it's actually 93, which is 90 +3, so adding another 67\u00d73=201, so 6030+201=6231. Yep, same as before. \n\nAlternatively, I can think of 93 as 100 -7. So 67\u00d7100 = 6700, minus 67\u00d77 = 469. So 6700 - 469. Let's see: 6700 - 400 is 6300, minus 69 more is 6231. Again, the same result. \n\nAlright, so all methods are confirming that the product is 6231. I think that's solid. Initially, I thought I might have messed up the multiplication steps, but cross-verifying with different methods gives me confidence. \n\nJust to ensure there's no arithmetic mistake, let me do the standard algorithm again step by step:\n\nFirst step (3 \u00d7 67):\n\n3 \u00d7 7 = 21, write 1, carryover 2.\n\n3 \u00d7 6 = 18, plus 2 is 20. So first partial product is 201.\n\nSecond step (9 \u00d7 67, but shifted one position left because it's the tens place):\n\n9 \u00d77 = 63, write 3, carryover 6.\n\n9 \u00d76 = 54, plus 6 is 60. So the second partial product is 603, but shifted left becomes 6030.\n\nAdding 201 + 6030:\n\n201 + 6000 = 6201,\n\n6201 + 30 = 6231. Yep, exactly.\n\nTherefore, the product of 67 and 93 is indeed 6231. No mistakes detected in the calculations. All different methods lead to the same result. I'm pretty confident now that this is correct.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 67 and 93 is calculated as follows:\n\n1. **Using the standard multiplication algorithm:**\n   - Multiply 67 by 3 (ones place of 93):\n     ```\n       67\n     \u00d7  3\n     ----\n      201\n     ```\n   - Multiply 67 by 9 (tens place of 93, shifted left by one position):\n     ```\n       67\n     \u00d7 90\n     ----\n     6030\n     ```\n   - Add the partial products:\n     ```\n       201\n     +6030\n     ----\n      6231\n     ```\n\n2. **Verification using the distributive property:**\n   - Break down the numbers:  \n     \\[\n     (60 + 7)(90 + 3) = 60\u00d790 + 60\u00d73 + 7\u00d790 + 7\u00d73\n     \\]\n   - Calculate each term:\n     \\[\n     60\u00d790 = 5400,\\quad 60\u00d73 = 180,\\quad 7\u00d790 = 630,\\quad 7\u00d73 = 21\n     \\]\n   - Sum the results:\n     \\[\n     5400 + 180 + 630 + 21 = 6231\n     \\]\n\n3. **Alternative method (rounding adjustment):**\n   - Compute \\(67 \\times 90 = 6030\\), then add \\(67 \\times 3 = 201\\):\n     \\[\n     6030 + 201 = 6231\n     \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**  \nThe product of 67 and 93 is \\boxed{6231}.",
