tens place): 44\u00d750=2200\n\nAdd them together: 2200 + 264 = 2464.\n\nAlternatively, another method: 44 \u00d7 56 can be thought of as (40 + 4)(50 + 6). Let's expand that:\n\n40\u00d750 = 2000\n\n40\u00d76 = 240\n\n4\u00d750 = 200\n\n4\u00d76 =24\n\nAdd them all: 2000 + 240 = 2240; 2240 +200 =2440; 2440 +24=2464. Same result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the difference of squares? Let me see:\n\nNotice that 44 and 56 are equidistant from 50? Wait, 44 is 6 less, 56 is 6 more. So, 44\u00d756 = (50 -6)(50 +6) = 50\u00b2 -6\u00b2 = 2500 -36 = 2464. Oh, that's a clever way.\n\nYes, that gives the same answer. So 2464 is the correct product.\n\nWait a second, but in my earlier incorrect thought process when I was confused with 30 and 09, I got conflicting answers, but now with the correct numbers, the methods all concur to 2464. So the answer should be 2464.\n\nWait, but let me confirm with another method. Let me do 44 multiplied by 56 step by step:\n\n44 \u00d7 56:\n\nMultiply 44 by 6 units: 44\u00d76=264.\n\nMultiply 44 by 50: as before, 2200.\n\nAdding them gives 264 + 2200 = 2464.\n\nAlternatively, using the standard vertical multiplication:\n\n   44\n\u00d7 56\n-------\nFirst line: 44\u00d76 = 264\n\nSecond line: 44\u00d750 = 2200 (shifted one position to the left)\n\nAdd: 264 + 2200 = 2464.\n\nYes, that's consistent.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using calculator verification? Since I can't use a calculator, but let's see:\n\n44 \u00d7 50 is 2200, plus 44 \u00d76 is 264, so total 2200+264=2464. Yep.\n\nSo the correct answer is 2464. The earlier confusion was because in my thought process I was mixing up numbers (30 and 09 vs 44 and 56), but focusing on the actual question, it's 44 \u00d756=2464.\n\nWait, just to ensure, let me try another approach:\n\n44 \u00d7 56 = (40 +4)(50 +6) = 40\u00d750 +40\u00d76 +4\u00d750 +4\u00d76 = 2000 +240 +200 +24 = 2000+240 is 2240, plus 200 is 2440, plus 24 is 2464. Same result.\n\nAlternatively, 56\u00d744 can be written as 56\u00d74\u