lus 30 is 1830. Yep, same result. \n\nI think 1830 is the correct answer. Wait, let me check with a calculator approach. \n\n61 multiplied by 30: 61*30. 61*3 is 183, so times 10 is 1830. \n\nYes, that's consistent. I think my initial confusion was because I started thinking about a different problem (96*07) by mistake, but now focusing on 61*30, it's clear. The answer should be 1830.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 61 and 30 is calculated as follows:\n\n\\[\n61 \\times 30 = 61 \\times (3 \\times 10) = (61 \\times 3) \\times 10\n\\]\n\nFirst, compute \\(61 \\times 3\\):\n\\[\n61 \\times 3 = 183\n\\]\n\nThen multiply by 10:\n\\[\n183 \\times 10 = 1830\n\\]\n\n**Answer:** \\(\\boxed{1830}\\)",
