860.\n\nAdding 81 +4860:\n\n4860 +80 is 4940, plus 1 more is 4941. Yep.\n\nAlright, that's consistent. I think that's thorough enough. The answer is 4941.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 81 and 61 is \\boxed{4941}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 81 and 61, we can use multiple methods to ensure accuracy:\n\n1. **Difference of Squares**:\n   - Recognize that 81 and 61 can be expressed as \\(71 + 10\\) and \\(71 - 10\\) respectively.\n   - Using the formula \\((a + b)(a - b) = a^2 - b^2\\):\n     \\[\n     (71 + 10)(71 - 10) = 71^2 - 10^2\n     \\]\n   - Calculate \\(71^2\\):\n     \\[\n     71^2 = (70 + 1)^2 = 70^2 + 2 \\cdot 70 \\cdot 1 + 1^2 = 4900 + 140 + 1 = 5041\n     \\]\n   - Subtract \\(10^2\\):\n     \\[\n     5041 - 100 = 4941\n     \\]\n\n2. **Distributive Property**:\n   - Break down the numbers:\n     \\[\n     81 \\times 61 = (80 + 1)(60 + 1)\n     \\]\n   - Expand using the distributive property:\n     \\[\n     80 \\times 60 + 80 \\times 1 + 1 \\times 60 + 1 \\times 1 = 4800 + 80 + 60 + 1 = 4941\n     \\]\n\n3. **Direct Multiplication**:\n   - Multiply 81 by 61 step-by-step:\n     \\[\n     81 \\times 61 = 81 \\times (60 + 1) = 81 \\times 60 + 81 \\times 1 = 4860 + 81 = 4941\n     \\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 81 and 61 is \\(\\boxed{4941}\\).",
