 4 = 8, plus the carried 1 is 9. So the second partial product is 900 (since we shifted left by one).\n\nNow add the two partial products:\n\n225\n\n+900\n\n= 1125.\n\nSo the product is 1125. Let me verify this with another method to be sure.\n\nAlternatively, we can use the distributive property: 45 \u00d7 25 = (40 + 5) \u00d7 25 = 40\u00d725 + 5\u00d725.\n\nCalculating each part:\n\n40 \u00d7 25 = 1000 (since 40\u00d725 is like 10\u00d74\u00d725 = 10\u00d7100 = 1000),\n\n5 \u00d7 25 = 125,\n\nAdding them together: 1000 + 125 = 1125. Same result.\n\nAnother way: 25 is a quarter of 100, so 45 \u00d7 25 = 45 \u00d7 (100/4) = (45/4) \u00d7 100. But 45 divided by 4 is 11.25, so 11.25 \u00d7 100 = 1125. Yep, that works too.\n\nAlternatively, breaking down both numbers into prime factors:\n\n45 = 9 \u00d7 5 = 3\u00b2 \u00d7 5,\n\n25 = 5\u00b2.\n\nMultiplying them together: 3\u00b2 \u00d7 5 \u00d7 5\u00b2 = 3\u00b2 \u00d7 5\u00b3 = 9 \u00d7 125 = 1125. Yep.\n\nHmm, all methods lead to 1125, so that must be the correct answer. Earlier confusion was because I misread the original numbers in my thinking process. Good thing I caught that and started over properly.\n\nSo the final answer should be 1125.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 45 and 25 is calculated as follows:\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n1. **Direct Multiplication:**\n   - Multiply 45 by 5 (the ones digit of 25):\n     \\[\n     45 \\times 5 = 225\n     \\]\n   - Multiply 45 by 20 (the tens digit of 25, treated as \\(2 \\times 10\\)):\n     \\[\n     45 \\times 20 = 900\n     \\]\n   - Add the two results:\n     \\[\n     225 + 900 = 1125\n     \\]\n\n2. **Using Distributive Property:**\n   - Break down \\(45 \\times 25\\) into \\((40 + 5) \\times 25\\):\n     \\[\n     40 \\times 25 = 1000 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 5 \\times 25 = 125\n     \\]\n   - Sum the parts:\n     \\[\n     1000 + 125 = 1125\n     \\]\n\n**Final Answer:** \\(\\boxed{1125}\\)",
