xed{4512}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 47 and 96, we can use the distributive property by breaking down 96 into 100 - 4:\n\n\\[\n47 \\times 96 = 47 \\times (100 - 4) = 47 \\times 100 - 47 \\times 4\n\\]\n\nCalculating each term separately:\n\\[\n47 \\times 100 = 4700\n\\]\n\\[\n47 \\times 4 = 188\n\\]\n\nSubtracting these results:\n\\[\n4700 - 188 = 4512\n\\]\n\nTo verify, we can use the standard multiplication method:\n\\[\n47 \\times 96 = 47 \\times (90 + 6) = (47 \\times 90) + (47 \\times 6)\n\\]\n\nCalculating each term separately:\n\\[\n47 \\times 90 = 4230\n\\]\n\\[\n47 \\times 6 = 282\n\\]\n\nAdding these results:\n\\[\n4230 + 282 = 4512\n\\]\n\nAnother verification by breaking down 47 into 40 + 7:\n\\[\n47 \\times 96 = (40 + 7) \\times 96 = (40 \\times 96) + (7 \\times 96)\n\\]\n\nCalculating each term separately:\n\\[\n40 \\times 96 = 3840\n\\]\n\\[\n7 \\times 96 = 672\n\\]\n\nAdding these results:\n\\[\n3840 + 672 = 4512\n\\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 47 and 96 is \\boxed{4512}.",
