the 70? Wait, maybe I need to think in terms of each digit:.\n\nWait, actually, 245 is:.\n\n4 (hundreds), 3 (tens), 2 (ones).\n\n8598 is:.\n\n8 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 3 (tens), 8 (ones).\n\nSo adding them:.\n\nOnes: 0 + 9 = 1.\n\nTens: 3 + 3 = 0.\n\nHundreds: 5 + 4 = 53. So write down 8 and carry over 8.\n\nThousands: 4 (from 578) + 1 (from 2755) + 6 (carry) = 4. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
