0d74=256, then \u00d710).  \n\n64\u00d73 = 192.  \n\n2560 - 192 = 2368.  \n\nYep, same answer. So I think the correct product is 2368. The initial confusion was because I started with a different problem but caught it and recalculated properly.  \n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 64 and 37 is \\boxed{2368}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 64 and 37, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. Multiply 64 by 7:\n   \\[\n   64 \\times 7 = 448\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 64 by 30 (since the 3 in 37 is in the tens place):\n   \\[\n   64 \\times 30 = 1920\n   \\]\n\n3. Add the results of the two multiplications:\n   \\[\n   448 + 1920 = 2368\n   \\]\n\nTo verify, we can use the distributive property by breaking down the numbers:\n\\[\n64 \\times 37 = (60 + 4)(30 + 7)\n\\]\nUsing the FOIL method:\n- First: \\(60 \\times 30 = 1800\\)\n- Outer: \\(60 \\times 7 = 420\\)\n- Inner: \\(4 \\times 30 = 120\\)\n- Last: \\(4 \\times 7 = 28\\)\n\nAdding these results together:\n\\[\n1800 + 420 + 120 + 28 = 2368\n\\]\n\nAnother verification using the distributive property:\n\\[\n64 \\times 37 = 64 \\times (40 - 3) = 64 \\times 40 - 64 \\times 3\n\\]\n\\[\n64 \\times 40 = 2560 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 64 \\times 3 = 192\n\\]\n\\[\n2560 - 192 = 2368\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 64 and 37 is \\boxed{2368}.",
