 I switched to 25 and 46. That's an inconsistency because I misread the numbers. I need to correct that.\n\nOkay, let's start over properly. The problem is 37 \u00d7 89.\n\nHmm, how should I approach this? Let me try the standard multiplication algorithm again, but this time with the correct numbers.\n\nWriting it down:\n\n```.\n    37\n  \u00d7 89\n  -------\n```.\n\nMultiplying 37 by 9 (the units digit of 89):\n\n7\u00d79 = 63. Write down 3, carry over 6.\n\n3\u00d79 = 27, plus the carried 6 is 33. So the first partial product is 333.\n\nThen multiplying 37 by 80 (the tens digit of 89, so it's 8\u00d710):\n\nFirst, multiply 37 by 8:\n\n7\u00d78 = 56. Write down 6, carry over 5.\n\n3\u00d78 = 24, plus the 5 is 29. So that gives 296. But since we're multiplying by the tens place, we need to shift one position to the left, so it becomes 2960.\n\nNow add the two partial products: 333 + 2960.\n\nAdding them together:\n\n333 + 2960:\n\n3 + 0 = 3 (units place)\n\n3 + 6 = 9 (tens place)\n\n3 + 9 = 12 (hundreds place, write down 2, carry over 1)\n\nNow the thousands place: 2 + 0 (since 333 has no thousands) plus the carried 1 is 3.\n\nWait, actually, 2960 is 2 thousands, 9 hundreds, 6 tens, 0 ones. Adding to 0333:\n\nUnits: 3 + 0 = 3\n\nTens: 3 + 6 = 9\n\nHundreds: 3 + 9 = 12 (write 2, carry 1)\n\nThousands: 2 (from 2960) + 1 (carry) = 3.\n\nSo total is 3293?\n\nWait, let me add them numerically:\n\n333\n\n+2960\n\n=?\n\n333 + 2960:\n\n333 + 2000 = 2333\n\n2333 + 960 = 2333 + 900 = 3233, then +60 = 3293. Yes, so total is 3293.\n\nBut let me verify this with another method to be sure. Let's use the distributive property again.\n\n37 \u00d7 89 can be expressed as (30 + 7) \u00d7 (80 + 9).\n\nExpanding this:\n\n30\u00d780 + 30\u00d79 + 7\u00d780 + 7\u00d79.\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n30\u00d780 = 2400.\n\n30\u00d79 = 270.\n\n7\u00d780 = 560.\n\n7\u00d79 = 63.\n\nAdding all together:\n\n2400 + 270 = 2670.\n\n560 + 63 = 623.\n\nThen 2670 + 623: 2670 + 600 = 3270, plus 23 is 3293. So that matches.\n\nAlternatively, another way: 37 \u00d7 90 = 3330, then subtract 37 to get 3330 - 37 = 3293. Yep, that works too.\n\nSo the correct product is 3293.\n\nWait, but in my first incorrect attempt I had confusion with different numbers, but after correcting, the answer is 3293.\n\nTherefore, the answer should be 3293. Let me just confirm with another method: calculator style.\n\nMultiplying 37 by 89:\n\nFirst, 37 \u00d7 80 = 2960.\n\n37 \u00d79= 333.\n\nAdding 2960 + 333 = 3293. Correct.\n\nSo, after correcting my initial misread of the problem and carefully redoing the calculations, the product of 37 and 89 is indeed 3293.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 37 and 89 is \\boxed{3293}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 37 and 89, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n   37 \\\\\n\\times 89 \\\\\n\\hline\n   333 \\quad \\text{(37 \u00d7 9)} \\\\\n+2960 \\quad \\text{(37 \u00d7 80, shifted one position to the left)} \\\\\n\\hline\n  3293 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nBreaking it down step-by-step:\n1. Multiply 37 by 9:\n   \\[\n   37 \\times 9 = 333\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 37 by 80 (which is 8 \u00d7 10):\n   \\[\n   37 \\times 80 = 2960\n   \\]\n3. Add the partial products:\n   \\[\n   333 + 2960 = 3293\n   \\]\n\nVerification using the distributive property:\n\\[\n(30 + 7) \\times (80 + 9) = 30 \\times 80 + 30 \\times 9 + 7 \\times 80 + 7 \\times 9\n\\]\n\\[\n= 2400 + 270 + 560 + 63 = 2400 + 270 = 2670; \\quad 560 + 63 = 623\n\\]\n\\[\n2670 + 623 = 3293\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 37 and 89 is \\boxed{3293}.",
