2 is 16.\n\nAdding all those together: 2000 +100 =2100; 2100 +320=2420; 2420 +16=2436. Same result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe break it down as 58*42 = (60 -2)*42 = 60*42 -2*42 = 2520 -84 = 2436. Yep, that works too.\n\nSo the correct answer should be 2436. I need to make sure I didn't make any calculation mistakes here. Let me verify once more.\n\n60 times 42 is indeed 2520 (since 60*40=2400 and 60*2=120; 2400+120=2520). Subtract 2*42=84, so 2520-84 is 2436. Correct.\n\nAnother way: 58*42. Let's do 50*42 +8*42. 50*42 is 2100 (50*40=2000, 50*2=100; total 2100). 8*42 is 336. Then 2100 +336 is 2436. Yep.\n\nAlright, all methods give me 2436. So the product of 58 and 42 is 2436. I just need to make sure I didn't have any arithmetic errors here. Let me check the first method again:\n\n58 times 2 is 116. 58 times 40 is 2320. Adding them: 2320 +100 is 2420, plus 16 is 2436. Correct.\n\nOkay, so the answer is definitely 2436. I initially messed up because I thought it was 36 and 42, but after realizing the correct numbers, it all checks out. Phew!\n</think>\n\nThe product of 58 and 42 can be calculated using the standard multiplication method:\n\n```\n   58\n\u00d7 42\n-----\n  116  (58 \u00d7 2)\n+2320  (58 \u00d7 40, shifted one position to the left)\n-----\n  2436\n```\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n1. Multiply 58 by 2 (units place of 42):  \n   \\(58 \\times 2 = 116\\).\n2. Multiply 58 by 40 (tens place of 42):  \n   \\(58 \\times 40 = 2320\\).\n3. Add the results from steps 1 and 2:  \n   \\(116 + 2320 = 2436\\).\n\n**Final Answer:**  \n\\boxed{2436}",
