utive property by recognizing that 99 is 100 minus 1:\n\n\\[\n99 \\times 67 = (100 - 1) \\times 67 = 100 \\times 67 - 1 \\times 67\n\\]\n\nBreaking this down:\n\\[\n100 \\times 67 = 6,\\!700\n\\]\n\\[\n1 \\times 67 = 67\n\\]\n\nSubtract the second result from the first:\n\\[\n6,\\!700 - 67 = 6,\\!633\n\\]\n\n**Verification using standard multiplication:**\n- Multiply 99 by 7 (units place):  \n  \\(99 \\times 7 = 693\\)\n- Multiply 99 by 60 (tens place):  \n  \\(99 \\times 60 = 5,\\!940\\)\n- Add the results:  \n  \\(693 + 5,\\!940 = 6,\\!633\\)\n\n**Final Answer:**  \nThe product of 99 and 67 is \\(\\boxed{6633}\\).",
