ll those together: 7200 + 480 = 7680; 7680 +270=7950; 7950 +18=7968. Yep, same answer.\n\nAnother way: Maybe using the difference of squares? Let's see if that's possible. Hmm, 83 and 96 are not symmetric around a common number, but let's see:\n\nAlternatively, 83\u00d796 = (80 +3)(100 -4). Maybe that's more complicated?\n\n80\u00d7100=8000; 80\u00d7(-4)= -320\n\n3\u00d7100=300; 3\u00d7(-4)= -12\n\nTotal: 8000 -320 +300 -12 = 8000 -320 is 7680; 7680 +300 is 7980; 7980 -12 is 7968. Still the same.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the complement method? For example, 96 is close to 100. Let me think:\n\nBut maybe it's overcomplicating. Since standard multiplication gives 7968 and cross-verified with multiple methods, I can be confident that's the correct answer.\n\nTherefore, the product of 83 and 96 is 7968.\n\nWait, but let me just do a quick check with approximate calculation. 80\u00d795 is 7600, and 83 is 3 more than 80, so 3\u00d795=285, so 7600 +285=7885. But 96 is 1 more than 95, so actually, the original difference is 83\u00d7(95+1) = 7885 +83 = 7968. So that approximation also confirms it.\n\nAlright, I think that's solid. So the answer should be 7968.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 83 and 96 is \\boxed{7968}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 83 and 96, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. Multiply 83 by 6 (the units digit of 96):\n   \\[\n   83 \\times 6 = 498\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 83 by 90 (the tens digit of 96, which is 9 \u00d7 10):\n   \\[\n   83 \\times 9 = 747 \\quad \\text{(then multiply by 10)} \\quad 747 \\times 10 = 7470\n   \\]\n3. Add the two partial products:\n   \\[\n   498 + 7470 = 7968\n   \\]\n\nTo verify, we can use the distributive property:\n\\[\n83 \\times 96 = 83 \\times (90 + 6) = 83 \\times 90 + 83 \\times 6 = 7470 + 498 = 7968\n\\]\n\nAnother verification using the distributive property with expanded form:\n\\[\n(80 + 3)(90 + 6) = 80 \\times 90 + 80 \\times 6 + 3 \\times 90 + 3 \\times 6\n\\]\n\\[\n= 7200 + 480 + 270 + 18 = 7200 + 480 = 7680; \\quad 7680 + 270 = 7950; \\quad 7950 + 18 = 7968\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 83 and 96 is \\boxed{7968}.",
