ain the steps clearly now that I have the right numbers.\n\nFirst, recognize that multiplying by 50 is the same as multiplying by 5 and then by 10. So breaking it down:\n\n14 \u00d7 5 = 70. Then, 70 \u00d7 10 = 700. Alternatively, since 50 has a zero, you can multiply 14 by 5 (which is 70) and then add a zero at the end, resulting in 700. Both methods lead to the same answer. Therefore, the product of 14 and 50 is 700.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 14 and 50 is \\boxed{700}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 14 and 50, we can use the following steps:\n\n1. Recognize that multiplying by 50 is the same as multiplying by 5 and then by 10.\n2. First, calculate \\(14 \\times 5\\):\n   \\[\n   14 \\times 5 = 70\n   \\]\n3. Then, multiply the result by 10:\n   \\[\n   70 \\times 10 = 700\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 14 and 50 is \\(\\boxed{700}\\).",
