s in my initial steps, probably due to rushing or confusing the numbers. It's important to break it down properly and check each step carefully.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 70 and 24 is calculated as follows:\n\n1. **Breakdown Method**:\n   - Multiply 70 by 20:  \n     \\(70 \\times 20 = 1400\\)\n   - Multiply 70 by 4:  \n     \\(70 \\times 4 = 280\\)\n   - Add the results:  \n     \\(1400 + 280 = 1680\\)\n\n2. **Alternative Verification**:\n   - Use \\(24 \\times 7 \\times 10\\):  \n     \\(24 \\times 7 = 168\\)  \n     \\(168 \\times 10 = 1680\\)\n\nBoth methods confirm the **final answer**:  \n\\(\\boxed{1680}\\)",
