ght of as 94 x (70 +5) = 94x70 +94x5. Which is the same as above.\n\nAlternatively, since 75 is 3/4 of 100, so 94 x75 = 94 x (3/4 x100) = (94 x 3)/4 x100. But that might complicate. Alternatively, 94 x75 = (90 +4)x75 = 90x75 +4x75.\n\n90x75: 90x70 =6300, 90x5=450, so total 6750.\n\n4x75=300. So total is 6750 +300=7050.\n\nYes, consistent.\n\nAlternatively, maybe 75 is 25 times 3, so 94x25x3. 94x25: 94x100/4 = 9400/4 =2350. Then 2350x3=7050. That works.\n\nSo all methods point to 7050. So the correct answer should be 7050.\n\nBut in my first approach I was confused with different numbers, but after correcting the problem, it's clear. So the product is 7050.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 94 and 75 is \\boxed{7050}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 94 and 75, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm or the distributive property. Here, we use the distributive property for clarity:\n\n1. Break down the numbers using the distributive property:\n   \\[\n   94 \\times 75 = (90 + 4) \\times (70 + 5)\n   \\]\n2. Expand the product:\n   \\[\n   90 \\times 70 + 90 \\times 5 + 4 \\times 70 + 4 \\times 5\n   \\]\n3. Calculate each term:\n   \\[\n   90 \\times 70 = 6300\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   90 \\times 5 = 450\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   4 \\times 70 = 280\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   4 \\times 5 = 20\n   \\]\n4. Sum the results of each term:\n   \\[\n   6300 + 450 + 280 + 20 = 6300 + 450 = 6750\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   6750 + 280 = 7030\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   7030 + 20 = 7050\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 94 and 75 is \\boxed{7050}.",
