again. 90 times 50 is 4500, plus 90 times 4 is 360, plus 1 times 50 is 50, plus 1 times 4 is 4. 4500+360=4860, plus 50 is 4910, plus 4 is 4914. Yep, that's correct.\n\nSo I think the answer is 4914. I need to make sure I didn't confuse any numbers. Let me try another way: 54 times 90 is 4860, plus 54 more (since it's 91 instead of 90), so 4860 +54=4914. Exactly. Okay, definitely that's the right answer.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 91 and 54 can be calculated using the distributive property or standard multiplication:\n\n**Method 1: Distributive Property**  \nBreak down the numbers:  \n\\[\n91 \\times 54 = (90 + 1)(50 + 4)\n\\]  \nMultiply each term:  \n\\[\n= 90 \\times 50 + 90 \\times 4 + 1 \\times 50 + 1 \\times 4\n\\]  \nCalculate each part:  \n\\[\n= 4500 + 360 + 50 + 4\n\\]  \nAdd the results:  \n\\[\n4500 + 360 = 4860 \\\\\n4860 + 50 = 4910 \\\\\n4910 + 4 = 4914\n\\]\n\n**Method 2: Standard Multiplication**  \n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n   91 \\\\\n\\times 54 \\\\\n\\hline\n   364 \\quad (\\text{91 \u00d7 4}) \\\\\n+4550 \\quad (\\text{91 \u00d7 50}) \\\\\n\\hline\n  4914 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n**Final Answer:**  \nThe product of 91 and 54 is \\(\\boxed{4914}\\).",
