 is 2920, minus 70 is 2850, minus 3 is 2847. Same result.\n\nAnother way: Maybe use 73*40 = 2920, then subtract 73 once, so 2920 -73 = 2847. Yep, that works.\n\nSo the product is 2847. I think that's correct. Let me check with a calculator method.\n\nAlternatively, 39 multiplied by 70 is 2730, and 39 multiplied by 3 is 117. Adding those together gives 2730 + 117 = 2847. Yep, that's the same as before. So I think that's the right answer.\n\nWait, but in my initial thinking process, I started with 16 and 95? How did that happen? Maybe I misread the problem initially. But after correcting myself, I arrived at 2847. So the final answer should be 2847. Let me confirm once again.\n\n39 times 73:\n\n39 x 70 = 2730,\n\n39 x 3 = 117,\n\n2730 + 117 = 2847. Correct.\n\nAlternatively, 73 x 40 = 2920, subtract 73 gives 2920 -73 = 2847. Yep.\n\nTherefore, the answer is 2847.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 39 and 73 is calculated as follows:\n\n**Step 1:** Break down the multiplication using the distributive property:  \n\\[\n39 \\times 73 = (40 - 1) \\times (70 + 3)\n\\]\n\n**Step 2:** Expand the terms:  \n\\[\n= 40 \\times 70 + 40 \\times 3 - 1 \\times 70 - 1 \\times 3\n\\]\n\n**Step 3:** Calculate each part:  \n\\[\n40 \\times 70 = 2800, \\quad 40 \\times 3 = 120, \\quad 1 \\times 70 = 70, \\quad 1 \\times 3 = 3\n\\]\n\n**Step 4:** Combine the results:  \n\\[\n2800 + 120 - 70 - 3 = 2800 + 120 = 2920 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 2920 - 70 = 2850 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 2850 - 3 = 2847\n\\]\n\n**Verification using standard multiplication:**  \n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n\\quad \\ 39 \\\\\n\\times 73 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\quad 117 \\quad (\\text{39 \u00d7 3}) \\\\\n+ 2730 \\quad (\\text{39 \u00d7 70}) \\\\\n\\hline\n\\quad 2847 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n**Final Answer:**  \n\\[\n\\boxed{2847}\n\\]",
