n3. Add the results of the two multiplications:\n   \\[\n   234 + 2080 = 2314\n   \\]\n\nVerification using the distributive property:\n1. Break down the numbers:\n   \\[\n   26 \\times 89 = (20 + 6) \\times (80 + 9)\n   \\]\n2. Expand using the distributive property:\n   \\[\n   20 \\times 80 + 20 \\times 9 + 6 \\times 80 + 6 \\times 9\n   \\]\n3. Calculate each term:\n   \\[\n   20 \\times 80 = 1600\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   20 \\times 9 = 180\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   6 \\times 80 = 480\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   6 \\times 9 = 54\n   \\]\n4. Sum the results:\n   \\[\n   1600 + 180 + 480 + 54 = 2314\n   \\]\n\nAnother verification method:\n1. Calculate \\(26 \\times 90\\) and subtract 26:\n   \\[\n   26 \\times 90 = 2340\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   2340 - 26 = 2314\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 26 and 89 is \\(\\boxed{2314}\\).",
