vely, using the distributive property:\n\n45 \u00d7 41 = (40 + 5)(40 + 1)\n\nExpanding this:\n\n40\u00d740 + 40\u00d71 + 5\u00d740 + 5\u00d71\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n40\u00d740 = 1600\n\n40\u00d71 = 40\n\n5\u00d740 = 200\n\n5\u00d71 = 5\n\nAdding them up: 1600 + 40 = 1640; 1640 + 200 = 1840; 1840 + 5 = 1845.\n\nSame result. So the correct answer is 1845. My initial confusion was because I misread the problem the first time, leading to incorrect intermediate steps. But upon carefully redoing it, it's clear that 45 multiplied by 41 is indeed 1845.\n\nAnother way to verify is using another method, such as the difference of squares or some other trick. Let's see if that's possible.\n\nNotice that 45 and 41 are both close to 43 (the average). Let me check the difference:\n\n45 = 43 + 2\n\n41 = 43 - 2\n\nWait, no, that's not quite accurate. The average of 45 and 41 is (45 + 41)/2 = 86/2 = 43. So yes, they are symmetric around 43. Therefore, their product can be written as (43 + 2)(43 - 2) = 43\u00b2 - (2)\u00b2.\n\nCalculating:\n\n43\u00b2 is 43\u00d743. Let's compute that:\n\n40\u00b2 = 1600,\n\n2\u00d740\u00d73 = 240,\n\n3\u00b2 = 9,\n\nSo (40+3)\u00b2 = 1600 + 240 + 9 = 1849.\n\nThen subtract 2\u00b2 = 4,\n\n1849 - 4 = 1845.\n\nSame answer again. So that confirms it. Therefore, the product of 45 and 41 is 1845.\n\nI think that's solid now. The key was realizing that my first attempts had incorrect numbers due to misreading, but after correcting that, all methods point to 1845. So I'm confident that's the right answer.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 45 and 41 is calculated as follows:\n\nUsing the standard multiplication method:\n```\n   45\n\u00d7 41\n-------\n    45   (45 \u00d7 1)\n+1800   (45 \u00d7 40, shifted one position left)\n-------\n  1845\n```\n\nAlternatively, using the distributive property:\n\\[\n45 \\times 41 = (40 + 5)(40 + 1) = 40 \\times 40 + 40 \\times 1 + 5 \\times 40 + 5 \\times 1 = 1600 + 40 + 200 + 5 = 1845\n\\]\n\nAnother verification via the difference of squares:\n\\[\n45 \\times 41 = (43 + 2)(43 - 2) = 43^2 - 2^2 = 1849 - 4 = 1845\n\\]\n\n**Answer:** The product of 45 and 41 is \\boxed{1845}.",
