 20\u00d72 =40, 7\u00d780=560, 7\u00d72=14. Adding all those together: 1600+40=1640, 1640+560=2200, then +14 gives 2214. That's consistent. So I think the first time I must have miscalculated because I confused the numbers or made an arithmetic error. The correct answer is 2214. \n\nWait, hold on again. Let me do the vertical multiplication again step by step to be absolutely sure. \n\n\u2003\u200327  \n\u2003\u00d782  \n\u2003------  \n\u2003\u202f??  \n\nFirst multiply 27 by 2 (units digit):\n\n2 \u00d7 7 = 14, write 4, carry 1.\n\n2 \u00d7 2 = 4, plus 1 is 5. So first partial product is 54.\n\nThen multiply 27 by 8 (tens digit). But since the 8 is in the tens place, it's actually 80, so we need to shift one position to the left.\n\n8 \u00d7 7 = 56, write 6, carry 5.\n\n8 \u00d7 2 = 16, plus 5 is 21. So the second partial product is 216 shifted left, so 2160.\n\nAdding 54 + 2160:\n\n2160  \n+\u00a0\u00a054  \n------  \n2214\n\nYes, that's correct. So my initial mistake was probably a miscalculation when I first did it, maybe I added wrong or multiplied wrong. But after verifying with different methods, the correct product is 2214. \n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use another check. Let's approximate. 27 is close to 30, and 82 is close to 80. 30\u00d780=2400. The actual answer should be a bit less, since 27 is 3 less than 30. So 2400 minus (3\u00d780)=2400-240=2160, but then also we have the 2 extra from the 82. Hmm, maybe this isn't the best approximation, but 2214 is indeed less than 2400, so that seems reasonable. \n\nAlternatively, let me divide 2214 by 27 and see if I get 82. 27\u00d780 is 2160, subtract that from 2214: 2214-2160=54. 54 divided by 27 is 2, so 80+2=82. Perfect, that checks out. \n\nAlternatively, divide 2214 by 82: 82\u00d720=1640, 2214-1640=574. 82\u00d77=574, so 20+7=27. Yep, that works too. \n\nSo after multiple checks, I'm confident the correct answer is 2214. My first method had an error in calculation, but the second method and subsequent checks confirm it. \n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 27 and 82 is \\boxed{2214}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 27 and 82, we can use the standard multiplication method:\n\n1. Write the numbers vertically:\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     \\quad 27 \\\\\n   \\times 82 \\\\\n   \\hline\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 27 by the units digit of 82 (which is 2):\n   \\[\n   27 \\times 2 = 54\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 27 by the tens digit of 82 (which is 8, representing 80), and shift the result one position to the left:\n   \\[\n   27 \\times 8 = 216 \\quad \\text{(then shift left to get 2160)}\n   \\]\n\n4. Add the two partial products together:\n   \\[\n   54 + 2160 = 2214\n   \\]\n\nVerification using the distributive property:\n- Break down the numbers: \\(27 \\times 82 = 27 \\times (80 + 2)\\)\n- Calculate each part:\n  \\[\n  27 \\times 80 = 2160 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 27 \\times 2 = 54\n  \\]\n- Add the results:\n  \\[\n  2160 + 54 = 2214\n  \\]\n\nFurther verification by division:\n- Dividing 2214 by 27 gives 82, and dividing 2214 by 82 gives 27, confirming the result.\n\nThus, the product of 27 and 82 is \\(\\boxed{2214}\\).",
