is calculated as follows:\n\n**Method 1: Using the 11's Multiplication Trick**\n- Write down the first digit (4) and the last digit (7).\n- Add the two digits: 4 + 7 = 11.\n- Place the sum (11) between the digits. Since 11 is two digits, carry over the 1:\n  - 4 (first digit) + 1 (carry) = 5.\n  - The middle digit becomes 1 (from 11).\n  - The last digit remains 7.\n\nResult: **517**.\n\n**Method 2: Standard Multiplication**\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n47 \\times 11 &= 47 \\times (10 + 1) \\\\\n&= 47 \\times 10 + 47 \\times 1 \\\\\n&= 470 + 47 \\\\\n&= 517.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\n**Final Answer:** \\boxed{517}",
