carried over 8? Wait, maybe I messed up the alignment. Let me check the addition again.\n\nWait, actually, when adding 483 and 7564, they should be aligned as:.\n\n\u2003\xa0619.\n+4595.\n------.\nBut actually, 157 is three digits, and 3962 is four digits. So:.\n\n\u2003\u2003196.\n+3776.\n--------.\nAligning the digits properly:.\n\n\u2003\u2003\xa0942.\n+7457.\n--------.\nStart from the rightmost digit:.\n\nOnes place: 2 + 2 = 0.\n\nTens place: 3 + 9 = 54, write 1, carryover 0.\n\nHundreds place: 8 + 5 = 6 plus the 2 carried over = 3.\n\nThousands place: 6 (from 643) + 3 = 0, plus no carryover, so 4.\n\nTen-thousands place: 7 from the 0347? Wait, 6514 is 4 thousands, 5 hundreds, 3 tens, 8 ones. Wait, actually, the 0 in 0441 is the thousands place. .\n\nWait, let me write them with commas for clarity:.\n\n054 is 9 hundreds, 1 tens, 4 ones.\n\n7719 is 1 thousands, 8 hundreds, 3 tens, 4 ones.\n\nSo when adding:.\n\n\u2003\xa0\xa0939.\n+9758.\n--------.\nAlign the digits:.\n\n\u2003\xa0782.\n+9568.\n--------.\nSo:.\n\nOnes: 3 + 1 = 4.\n\nTens: 6 + 6 = 43 (write 6, carryover 5).\n\nHundreds: 1 + 6 = 0 + 6 (carryover) = 7.\n\nThousands: 9 (from 116) +8 =9. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
