      "text": "841 + 4187 equals 88 + 1563.\n\nWait, hold on, maybe I messed up here. Let me recalculate step by step.\n\nWait, perhaps I should do this using the standard method again properly.\n\nWait first, maybe breaking down 37 and 97 into smaller parts would make it easier. Like using distributive property. So 37 times 97 is the same as 37*(90+7). Let's see: 37*90 plus 37*7. That might be easier. Let's compute those separately.\n\nFirst, 37 multiplied by 90. 37 times 9 is 333, so 37 times 90 is 3330.\n\nThen 37 multiplied by 7 is 259. Adding those together: 3330 + 259 = 3589?\n\nWait, but that doesn't seem right. Let me check again:\n\n37*90: 37*9 is 333, so adding a zero gives 3330. That's correct.\n\n37*7: 30*7=210 and 7*7=49, so 210+49=259. That's correct.\n\nAdding 3330 + 259: 3330 + 200 is 3530, then +59 is 3589. Hmm. Wait, but maybe I made a mistake here. Let me confirm by another method.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using the standard multiplication:\n\n37\n\ntimes 97:\n\nMultiply 37 by 7 first. 7*7 is 49, write down 9 and carryover 4. 3*7=21 plus 4 is 25. So first partial product is 259.\n\nThen, multiply 37 by 90 (since the 9 is in the tens place). So 37*90. To do that, multiply 37 by 9 again, which is 333, then add a zero at the end, making it 3330.\n\nNow add the two partial products: 259 + 3330 = 3589. So that's the same result as before. Hmm, so that's what I got.\n\nBut let me check with another method to be sure. Maybe using the standard algorithm step by step.\n\nLet me write it out:\n\n\u2003\u2003\u202f37\n\n\u00d7\u00a097\n\n________\n\nFirst, multiply 37 by 7: 37\u00d77 = 259. Write that down.\n\nThen, multiply 37 by 9 (which is actually 90, so we need to shift one position to the left). 37\u00d79 = 333, so shifted left becomes 3330.\n\nNow add 259 + 3330:\n\n259\n\n+3330\n\n______\n\n3589.\n\nYep, that's the same result. So the product is 3589?\n\nWait, hold on, but let me check using another approach. Maybe using (40 - 3)(100 - 3) and expanding that.\n\nWait, 37 is 40 - 3, and 97 is 100 - 3. So (a - b)(c - d) = ac - ad - bc + bd. Let's see.\n\nSo (40 - 3)(100 - 3) = 40\u00d7100 - 40\u00d73 - 3\u00d7100 + 3\u00d73.\n\nCompute each term:\n\n40\u00d7100 = 4000,\n\n40\u00d73 = 120,\n\n3\u00d7100 = 300,\n\n3\u00d73 = 9.\n\nSo putting it all together: 4000 - 120 - 300 + 9.\n\nCalculates as: 4000 minus 120 is 3880; 3880 minus 300 is 3580; 3580 plus 9 is 3589. So that's the same answer. Hmm, so that's consistent. So that's good.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use another method. Let me see. 37 \u00d7 97. Let me think of 97 as 100 - 3, so 37\u00d7(100 - 3) = 37\u00d7100 - 37\u00d73 = 3700 - 111 = 3589. Yep, that's another way. So 3700 minus 111 is 3589. That works too. So that also gives the same result.\n\nHmm, so all methods are pointing to 3589. But I want to make sure I didn't make any arithmetic errors here. Let me check again.\n\n37 \u00d7 100 is 3700. 37 \u00d7 3 is 111. So subtracting gives 3700 - 111 = 3589. Correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using calculator-like step-by-step:\n\n37 \u00d7 97.\n\nLet me do 37 \u00d7 90 = 3330 as before, then 37 \u00d7 7 = 259. Adding those gives 3330 + 259. 3330 + 200 is 3530, plus 59 is 3589. Correct.\n\nAlternatively, another way: 37 \u00d7 97. Let's see, 30 \u00d7 90 = 2700, 30\u00d77=210, 7\u00d790=630, 7\u00d77=49. Wait, no, that's breaking down both numbers into 30+7 and 90+7, which would be (30+7)(90+7) = 30\u00d790 + 30\u00d77 +7\u00d790 +7\u00d77. Let's compute that:\n\n30\u00d790 = 2700,\n\n30\u00d77 = 210,\n\n7\u00d790 = 630,\n\n7\u00d77 = 49.\n\nNow add them all: 2700 + 210 = 2910; 2910 + 630 = 3540; 3540 +49 = 3589. Yep, same result again. So all methods confirm that the product is 3589.\n\nWait a second, but just to make sure, let me do the multiplication step by step again:\n\n37\n\n\u00d797\n\nStart from the rightmost digit:\n\nFirst, 7 \u00d7 7 = 49. Write 9, carryover 4.\n\nNext, 7 \u00d7 3 = 21, plus the carried over 4 is 25. Write 25 next to the 9. So first partial product is 259.\n\nThen, moving to the second row (the 9 in 97 is in the tens place), so we need to shift one position to the left. So start with a zero or just shift. Let's do 9 \u00d77 = 63. Write down 3, carryover 6.\n\nThen 9 \u00d73 = 27 plus 6 is 33. So the second partial product is 333, but shifted one position left, so 3330.\n\nNow add 259 + 3330.\n\n259\n\n+3330\n\n= 3589. Correct.\n\nHmm, so I think that's consistent. So I think the answer is 3589.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can check using a calculator if I have one, but since I can't, I have to rely on cross-verification.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using another approach: 37\u00d797 = (35 +2) \u00d797 = 35\u00d797 + 2\u00d797. Let's see:\n\n35\u00d797: 30\u00d797 +5\u00d797.\n\n30\u00d797 = 2910,\n\n5\u00d797 = 485,\n\nSo 2910 +485= 3395.\n\nThen 2\u00d797=194,\n\nSo total is 3395 +194 = 3589. Yep, same result.\n\nAlternatively, 37\u00d797. Let me think of 37\u00d7100 which is 3700, then subtract 3\u00d737 which is 111. 3700-111 is 3589. That works too.\n\nAnother way: 97 is 96 +1, but maybe that complicates. Alternatively, 37\u00d797 = (40 -3)(97) = 40\u00d797 -3\u00d797. 40\u00d797 is 3880, 3\u00d797 is 291. 3880 -291 = 3589. Yep, that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, 97 is 90+7, so 37\u00d790 +37\u00d77 as done before.\n\nI think all methods are leading to the same answer, so I can be confident that the product of 37 and 97 is indeed 3589.\n\nWait, just to ensure there's no calculation mistake in any step. Let me do 37\u00d797 again step by step:\n\nStarting with:\n\nMultiply 37 by 7:\n\n7\u00d77=49, write 9, carryover 4.\n\nThen 3\u00d77=21 +4=25. So 259.\n\nThen multiply 37 by 9 (the 9 is in the tens place, so it's actually 90):\n\n9\u00d77=63, write 3, carryover 6.\n\n3\u00d79=27 +6=33. So that gives 333, but shifted left, so 3330.\n\nAdding 259 and 3330:\n\n259 + 3330. Let's see:\n\n259 + 3000 = 3259,\n\n3259 + 330 = 3589. Yep, that's right.\n\nAnother way: 3330 + 259. 3330 + 200 = 3530. Then add 59: 3530 + 59 = 3589.\n\nAlright, I think this is solid. I can't see any mistake here, so I believe the correct product is 3589.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 37 and 97 is \\boxed{3589}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 37 and 97, we can use multiple methods to ensure accuracy:\n\n1. **Distributive Property**:\n   - Break down 97 into 90 and 7:\n     \\[\n     37 \\times 97 = 37 \\times (90 + 7) = (37 \\times 90) + (37 \\times 7)\n     \\]\n   - Calculate each part:\n     \\[\n     37 \\times 90 = 3330 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 37 \\times 7 = 259\n     \\]\n   - Add the results:\n     \\[\n     3330 + 259 = 3589\n     \\]\n\n2. **Standard Multiplication Algorithm**:\n   - Multiply 37 by 7:\n     \\[\n     37 \\times 7 = 259\n     \\]\n   - Multiply 37 by 90 (shifted one position to the left):\n     \\[\n     37 \\times 90 = 3330\n     \\]\n   - Add the partial products:\n     \\[\n     259 + 3330 = 3589\n     \\]\n\n3. **Using the Difference of Squares**:\n   - Express 97 as \\(100 - 3\\) and apply the distributive property:\n     \\[\n     37 \\times 97 = 37 \\times (100 - 3) = 37 \\times 100 - 37 \\times 3\n     \\]\n   - Calculate each part:\n     \\[\n     37 \\times 100 = 3700 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 37 \\times 3 = 111\n     \\]\n   - Subtract the results:\n     \\[\n     3700 - 111 = 3589\n     \\]\n\nAll methods consistently yield the same result. Therefore, the product of 37 and 97 is \\(\\boxed{3589}\\).",
