      "text": "1234.\n\nWait, hold on a second. I feel like this might not be correct. Let me double-check using another method. Maybe the standard multiplication algorithm.\n\nLet me write down 45 on top and 87 below. But actually, the question was 45 times 87. Let me confirm. The user wrote: What is the Product of 45 and 87?\n\nYes, so 45 \u00d7 87. Alright, let me do this step by step properly.\n\nStarting with the standard multiplication:\n\n\u2003\u200345  \n\u00d7\u00a087  \n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500  \nFirst, multiply 45 by 7. 5\u00d77 is 35, write down 5 and carry over 3. Then 4\u00d77 is 28 plus the carried 3 is 31. So that gives 315.\n\nNext, multiply 45 by 80 (since the 8 is in the tens place, so it's 80). So 45 \u00d7 80. Let me compute that. 45 \u00d7 8 is 360, then add a zero at the end to make it 3600.\n\nThen add the two results: 315 + 3600. 315 + 3600 equals 3915.\n\nWait a second, so that's 3915? Let me check with another method to be sure.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using the distributive property again: 45 \u00d7 87 = (40 + 5) \u00d7 (80 + 7). Expanding this:\n\nFirst, multiply 40\u00d780 = 3200,\n\nthen 40\u00d77 = 280,\n\nthen 5\u00d780 = 400,\n\nand 5\u00d77 = 35.\n\nAdding all those together: 3200 + 280 is 3480, plus 400 is 3880, plus 35 is 3915. Okay, same result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can compute 45 \u00d7 87 as 45 \u00d7 (90 - 3) = 45\u00d790 - 45\u00d73. Let's see:\n\n45\u00d790: 45\u00d79 is 405, so times 10 is 4050,\n\n45\u00d73 is 135,\n\nso 4050 - 135 = 3915. Again the same answer.\n\nHmm, so why did I get confused earlier? I think I must have miscalculated in my first attempt when I was thinking of different numbers. The user's question is 45 and 87, so all these methods confirm that the product is 3915. Let me just make sure I didn't mix up any numbers in my head.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps using calculator verification, but since I can't use a calculator here, the multiple methods all leading to the same result give me confidence. Therefore, I think the correct product is 3915.\n\nBut wait, hold on, I just realized in my first part of thinking I was talking about 19\u00d774 and 28\u00d714, which might have been a mistake. The user's question is about 45\u00d787. Maybe I started thinking about a different problem initially but corrected myself. So the final answer after careful calculation is 3915.\n\nYes, that seems right. Let me write that as the final answer.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 45 and 87 is calculated as follows:\n\nUsing the standard multiplication method:  \n```\n   45  \n\u00d7  87  \n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500  \n  315   (45 \u00d7 7)  \n3600    (45 \u00d7 80, shifted one position to the left)  \n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500  \n3915  \n```\n\nAlternatively, using the distributive property:  \n\\[\n45 \\times 87 = (40 + 5) \\times (80 + 7) = 40 \\times 80 + 40 \\times 7 + 5 \\times 80 + 5 \\times 7  \n= 3200 + 280 + 400 + 35 = 3915\n\\]\n\n**Final Answer:**  \nThe product of 45 and 87 is \\boxed{3915}.",
