ther: 42 + 840 = 882.\n\nAlternatively, using calculator verification (pretending I'm using one):\n\n21 multiplied by 42. 20*40 is 800, 20*2 is 40, 1*40 is 40, 1*2 is 2. So adding those gives 800 +40+40+2=882.\n\nAll methods lead to 882. Therefore, the correct product is 882. \n\nI must have initially misread the question numbers, which led me to wrong calculations. But after correcting that, everything checks out. So the answer should be 882.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 21 and 42 is \\boxed{882}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 21 and 42, we can use the standard multiplication method:\n\n1. Write the numbers vertically:\n   ```\n    21\n  x 42\n  -----\n   ```\n\n2. Multiply 21 by 2 (the units digit of 42):\n   \\[\n   21 \\times 2 = 42\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 21 by 40 (the tens digit of 42, which is 4 in the tens place):\n   \\[\n   21 \\times 40 = 840\n   \\]\n\n4. Add the two results together:\n   \\[\n   42 + 840 = 882\n   \\]\n\nWe can also verify this using the distributive property:\n\\[\n21 \\times 42 = 21 \\times (40 + 2) = (21 \\times 40) + (21 \\times 2) = 840 + 42 = 882\n\\]\n\nAnother verification using the box method:\n- Breaking down 21 into 20 and 1, and 42 into 40 and 2:\n  \\[\n  \\begin{array}{c|cc}\n    & 20 & 1 \\\\\n  \\hline\n  40 & 800 & 40 \\\\\n  2 & 40 & 2 \\\\\n  \\end{array}\n  \\]\n- Summing all parts:\n  \\[\n  800 + 40 + 40 + 2 = 882\n  \\]\n\nThus, the product of 21 and 42 is \\boxed{882}.",
