where \\(a\\) is the average of the two numbers and \\(b\\) is half their difference:\n- The average of 45 and 41 is \\(\\frac{45 + 41}{2} = 43\\).\n- The difference between 45 and 41 is \\(45 - 41 = 4\\), so \\(b = \\frac{4}{2} = 2\\).\n\nThus, we can write:\n\\[\n45 = 43 + 2 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 41 = 43 - 2\n\\]\n\nUsing the difference of squares formula \\((a + b)(a - b) = a^2 - b^2\\):\n\\[\n45 \\times 41 = (43 + 2)(43 - 2) = 43^2 - 2^2\n\\]\n\nCalculating the squares:\n- \\(43^2 = 43 \\times 43 = 1849\\)\n- \\(2^2 = 4\\)\n\nSubtracting these results:\n\\[\n1849 - 4 = 1845\n\\]\n\nWe can also verify this using the standard multiplication method:\n\\[\n45 \\times 41 = 45 \\times (40 + 1) = 45 \\times 40 + 45 \\times 1 = 1800 + 45 = 1845\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 45 and 41 is \\(\\boxed{1845}\\).",
