nd{array}\n\\]\n\nBreaking it down step-by-step:\n1. Multiply 21 by 1 (the ones place of 61): \\(21 \\times 1 = 21\\).\n2. Multiply 21 by 60 (the tens place of 61): \\(21 \\times 60 = 1260\\).\n3. Add the results of the two multiplications: \\(21 + 1260 = 1281\\).\n\nVerification using the distributive property:\n\\[\n21 \\times 61 = 21 \\times (60 + 1) = (21 \\times 60) + (21 \\times 1) = 1260 + 21 = 1281\n\\]\n\nVerification using the FOIL method:\n\\[\n(20 + 1)(60 + 1) = 20 \\times 60 + 20 \\times 1 + 1 \\times 60 + 1 \\times 1 = 1200 + 20 + 60 + 1 = 1281\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 21 and 61 is \\(\\boxed{1281}\\).",
