 9300 -1581. Let's compute 9300 - 1581: 9300 -1500 =7800, then subtract 81 more: 7800 -81 = 7719. Yep, same result.\n\nAlright, so all methods are giving me 7719. Therefore, I think that's correct. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations, so I'm confident this is the right product.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 93 and 83 is \\boxed{7719}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 93 and 83, we can use multiple methods to verify the result:\n\n1. **Standard Multiplication:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     93 \\\\\n   \\times 83 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     279 \\quad (\\text{93} \\times 3) \\\\\n   +7440 \\quad (\\text{93} \\times 80) \\\\\n   \\hline\n     7719 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n   Adding the results of \\(93 \\times 3\\) and \\(93 \\times 80\\) gives \\(279 + 7440 = 7719\\).\n\n2. **Difference of Squares:**\n   \\[\n   93 \\times 83 = (88 + 5)(88 - 5) = 88^2 - 5^2\n   \\]\n   Calculating \\(88^2\\):\n   \\[\n   88^2 = (80 + 8)^2 = 80^2 + 2 \\times 80 \\times 8 + 8^2 = 6400 + 1280 + 64 = 7744\n   \\]\n   Subtracting \\(5^2\\) from \\(7744\\):\n   \\[\n   7744 - 25 = 7719\n   \\]\n\n3. **Distributive Property:**\n   \\[\n   93 \\times 83 = 93 \\times (80 + 3) = 93 \\times 80 + 93 \\times 3 = 7440 + 279 = 7719\n   \\]\n\n4. **Alternative Breakdown:**\n   \\[\n   93 \\times 83 = 93 \\times (100 - 17) = 93 \\times 100 - 93 \\times 17 = 9300 - 1581 = 7719\n   \\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 93 and 83 is \\(\\boxed{7719}\\).",
