s 1890.\n\nNow add 252 + 1890:\n\n252 + 1890 = 2142. Hmm, so the total is 2142? Let me verify with another method.\n\nUsing distributive property: 63 * 34 = (60 + 3)(30 +4) = 60*30 + 60*4 + 3*30 + 3*4 = 1800 + 240 + 90 + 12 = \n\nAdding them up: 1800 +240 is 2040, plus 90 is 2130, plus 12 is 2142. Okay, so that's consistent.\n\nAlternatively, 63*34 can be calculated as 63*(30+4)=63*30 +63*4. 63*30=1890, 63*4=252. 1890+252=2142. Correct.\n\nTherefore, the product is 2142. I think my confusion earlier was because I initially misread the numbers as 35 and 54, then corrected myself. So final answer should be 2142.\n\nBut let me double-check once more. Maybe using another method: 63*34.\n\nFirst, note that 63 is 7*9, and 34 is 2*17. But maybe not helpful. Alternatively, 34*60 = 2040, 34*3=102. So 2040 +102=2142. Yes. So that works.\n\nAlternatively, 34*63. Let me do it vertically again:\n\n   34\nx 63\n-----\n34*3=102\n\n34*60=2040\n\n2040 +102=2142. Yep, same result. Okay, so confident now that it's 2142.\n\nWait, the user's question was \"What is the Product of 63 and 34?\" so the answer is 2142. Alright, I think that's solid. I just had an initial mix-up with different numbers, but corrected myself. So the final answer is 2142.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 63 and 34 is \\boxed{2142}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 63 and 34, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. Multiply 63 by 4 (the units place of 34):\n   \\[\n   63 \\times 4 = 252\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 63 by 30 (the tens place of 34, represented as 3 shifted one position to the left):\n   \\[\n   63 \\times 30 = 1890\n   \\]\n3. Add the partial products together:\n   \\[\n   252 + 1890 = 2142\n   \\]\n\nVerification using the distributive property:\n\\[\n63 \\times 34 = (60 + 3)(30 + 4) = 60 \\times 30 + 60 \\times 4 + 3 \\times 30 + 3 \\times 4\n\\]\n\\[\n= 1800 + 240 + 90 + 12 = 1800 + 240 + 90 + 12 = 2142\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 63 and 34 is \\(\\boxed{2142}\\).",
