8 is 504, so times 10 is 5040. Correct.\n\n63\u00d73 is 189. Correct.\n\nAdding them: 5040 + 189. Let's see: 5040 + 100 = 5140; 5140 +89 = 5229. Correct.\n\nTherefore, the product is 5229.\n\nWait, but in my very first calculation when I was confused, I had 3559. That must have been from an incorrect multiplication. So I need to make sure that I didn't mix up any numbers here.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps I can compute 63\u00d783 step by step again:\n\nFirst, 63\u00d780:\n\n80 is 8\u00d710. 63\u00d78:\n\nCompute 60\u00d78=480, 3\u00d78=24. 480+24=504. Then 504\u00d710=5040.\n\nThen 63\u00d73=189. Adding together: 5040+189.\n\nLet me add 5040 + 200 = 5240, subtract 11 (since I added 11 extra) gives 5240 -11=5229. Correct.\n\nAlternatively, 5040 + 189:\n\nBreak down 189 into 100+80+9.\n\nSo 5040 + 100 = 5140.\n\n5140 +80 = 5220.\n\n5220 +9 =5229. Correct.\n\nSo all methods confirm that the product is 5229.\n\nTherefore, the answer should be 5229.\n\nWait a second, just to be absolutely sure, maybe I can do another check using estimation. Let's see, 60\u00d780=4800. 60\u00d783 is 4980. 63\u00d780 is 5040. So 63\u00d783 is a bit more than 5040. 5229 is 189 more than 5040, which makes sense because it's adding the 3\u00d763. So that's consistent. Alternatively, 63\u00d783 is (60+3)(80+3) = 60\u00d780 + 60\u00d73 + 3\u00d780 + 3\u00d73 = 4800+180+240+9= 4800+420+9=5229. Yep. That's right.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps I can do the multiplication vertically:\n\n\u2003\u200363\n\u00d7\u00a083\n-------\n\u2003189\u00a0 (63\u00d73)\n+5040\u00a0 (63\u00d780)\n-------\n\u20035229\n\nYes, that's correct.\n\nSo all methods lead to the same result. I think initially I confused myself by thinking of a different problem, but after correcting that, it's straightforward. Therefore, the product of 63 and 83 is 5229.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 63 and 83 is \\boxed{5229}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 63 and 83, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. Multiply 63 by 3 (the ones digit of 83):\n   \\[\n   63 \\times 3 = 189\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 63 by 80 (the tens digit of 83, which is equivalent to 80):\n   \\[\n   63 \\times 80 = 63 \\times 8 \\times 10 = (60 \\times 8 + 3 \\times 8) \\times 10 = (480 + 24) \\times 10 = 504 \\times 10 = 5040\n   \\]\n\n3. Add the two partial products together:\n   \\[\n   189 + 5040 = 5229\n   \\]\n\nWe can verify this using the distributive property:\n\\[\n(60 + 3)(80 + 3) = 60 \\times 80 + 60 \\times 3 + 3 \\times 80 + 3 \\times 3\n\\]\n\\[\n= 4800 + 180 + 240 + 9 = 4800 + 420 + 9 = 5229\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 63 and 83 is \\(\\boxed{5229}\\).",
