products together:\n\n   855\n+ 6,650\n--------\n  7,505\n\nWait, so adding 855 and 6,650: 855 + 6,650. Let's see, 6,650 + 800 is 7,450, then plus 55 is 7,505. That seems right.\n\nBut let me verify using another method to be sure. Maybe breaking down the numbers using distributive property:\n\n95 \u00d7 79 = (90 + 5) \u00d7 (70 + 9)\n\nExpanding this, we get:\n\n90\u00d770 + 90\u00d79 + 5\u00d770 + 5\u00d79\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n90\u00d770 = 6,300\n\n90\u00d79 = 810\n\n5\u00d770 = 350\n\n5\u00d79 = 45\n\nAdding all these together: 6,300 + 810 = 7,110; 350 + 45 = 395; then 7,110 + 395 = 7,505. Same result. Okay, that's a good check.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using another approach like the difference of squares? Let me think. Since 95 and 79 are both numbers around 87, but not sure if that helps. Alternatively, perhaps adjusting numbers to make them easier.\n\nFor example, 95 is 100 - 5, and 79 is 80 - 1. Let me try that:\n\n(100 - 5) \u00d7 (80 - 1) = 100\u00d780 - 100\u00d71 - 5\u00d780 + 5\u00d71\n\nWhich is 8,000 - 100 - 400 + 5 = 8,000 - 500 +5 = 7,505. Oh, that works too! That was a good method. So that confirms it again.\n\nHmm, so all methods are pointing to 7,505. Therefore, the product of 95 and 79 is 7,505.\n\nWait a second, but let me just do a quick estimation to ensure it's in the right ballpark. 95 is close to 100, and 79 is close to 80. So 100\u00d780 = 8,000. Our answer is 7,505, which is 500 less than 8,000. Since we subtracted 5 from 100 and 1 from 80, the difference makes sense because (100-5)(80-1) = 100\u00d780 - 100\u00d71 -5\u00d780 +5\u00d71, so subtracting those extra terms. So the estimation aligns. That gives me more confidence.\n\nAlternatively, if I had done 95*80, that would be 95*80 = 7,600. Then subtract 95 from that to get 95*(80 -1)= 7,600 -95 =7,505. Yep, that's another way.\n\nSo all methods are consistent. Therefore, I can be confident that the product of 95 and 79 is 7,505.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 95 and 79 is 