31^2\n\\]\n\nUsing the formula for squaring a binomial \\((a + b)^2 = a^2 + 2ab + b^2\\) where \\(a = 30\\) and \\(b = 1\\):\n\n\\[\n(30 + 1)^2 = 30^2 + 2(30)(1) + 1^2 = 900 + 60 + 1 = 961\n\\]\n\nAlternatively, using direct multiplication:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n   \\quad 31 \\\\\n\\times 31 \\\\\n\\hline\n   \\quad 31 \\quad (\\text{(31 \u00d7 1)}) \\\\\n+ 930 \\quad (\\text{(31 \u00d7 30, shifted left)}) \\\\\n\\hline\n   961 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n**Answer:** \\(\\boxed{961}\\)",
