ray}{r}\n    \\quad 97 \\\\\n   \\times 78 \\\\\n   \\hline\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 97 by the units digit of 78 (which is 8):\n   \\[\n   97 \\times 8 = 776\n   \\]\n   This gives the first partial product: 776.\n\n3. Multiply 97 by the tens digit of 78 (which is 7, representing 70) and shift the result one position to the left:\n   \\[\n   97 \\times 7 = 679\n   \\]\n   Shifting one position to the left gives 6790.\n\n4. Add the two partial products:\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n    \\quad 776 \\\\\n   + 6790 \\\\\n   \\hline\n    7566 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n\nVerification using the distributive property:\n\\[\n97 \\times 78 = (100 - 3)(70 + 8) = 100 \\times 70 + 100 \\times 8 - 3 \\times 70 - 3 \\times 8\n\\]\n\\[\n= 7000 + 800 - 210 - 24 = 7000 + 800 = 7800\n\\]\n\\[\n7800 - 210 = 7590\n\\]\n\\[\n7590 - 24 = 7566\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm the product is \\(\\boxed{7566}\\).",
