d by multiplying the two numbers together:\n\n\\[\n13 \\times 60 = 780\n\\]\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n1. **Break down the multiplication**:\n   - \\( 13 \\times 60 = 13 \\times (6 \\times 10) \\)\n   - Multiply \\( 13 \\times 6 = 78 \\)\n   - Then multiply by 10: \\( 78 \\times 10 = 780 \\)\n\n2. **Alternative method**:\n   - \\( 13 \\times 60 = (10 + 3) \\times 60 \\)\n   - \\( = 10 \\times 60 + 3 \\times 60 \\)\n   - \\( = 600 + 180 = 780 \\)\n\n**Final Answer:**  \nThe product of 13 and 60 is \\(\\boxed{780}\\).",
