n   19  \nx 19  \n------  \n  171  (19 \u00d7 9)  \n190   (19 \u00d7 1 shifted left by one position)  \n------  \n 361  \n\nAdding those two gives 361. \n\nTherefore, after correcting my initial misread of the problem, the correct product of 19 and 19 is 361. \n\nI think that's solid. Let me just check with a calculator method. Since I don't have a calculator here, but 20\u00d720 is 400, subtract 19 gives 381, but wait no, 20\u00d719 is 380, so 19\u00d719 is 380 minus 19, which is 361. Yup. \n\nAlternatively, 19 squared is known as a common square. 15\u00b2=225, 16\u00b2=256, 17\u00b2=289, 18\u00b2=324, 19\u00b2=361. So that progression makes sense. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 361. My initial confusion was because I misread the numbers, but after correcting that, everything checks out.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 19 and 19 is calculated as follows:  \n\n**Step 1:** Multiply 19 by 9 (units place of the second number):  \n\\[\n19 \\times 9 = 171\n\\]  \n\n**Step 2:** Multiply 19 by 10 (tens place of the second number, represented by the digit 1 shifted left):  \n\\[\n19 \\times 10 = 190\n\\]  \n\n**Step 3:** Add the results of the two partial products:  \n\\[\n171 + 190 = 361\n\\]  \n\n**Final Answer:**  \n\\[\n\\boxed{361}\n\\]",
