n\nWait, but just to be thorough, let me do the multiplication step by step as taught in school:\n\nMultiply 32 by 7 first:\n\n7\u00d72 =14, write down 4, carryover 1.\n\n7\u00d73 =21, plus 1 is 22. So first partial product is 224.\n\nThen multiply 32 by 70 (the 7 in the tens place):\n\nSo 7 (tens place) times 32 is 224, but shifted one position to the left, so 2240.\n\nAdding 224 and 2240 gives 2464. Yep, that's consistent. Okay, so confident now. The product is 2464.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 32 and 77 is \\boxed{2464}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 32 and 77, we can use the distributive property and break down the numbers:\n\n\\[\n32 \\times 77 = 32 \\times (70 + 7)\n\\]\n\nFirst, calculate \\(32 \\times 70\\):\n\n\\[\n32 \\times 70 = 32 \\times 7 \\times 10\n\\]\n\nBreaking down \\(32 \\times 7\\):\n\n\\[\n32 \\times 7 = (30 \\times 7) + (2 \\times 7) = 210 + 14 = 224\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\n\\[\n32 \\times 70 = 224 \\times 10 = 2240\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate \\(32 \\times 7\\):\n\n\\[\n32 \\times 7 = 224\n\\]\n\nAdding the two results together:\n\n\\[\n2240 + 224 = 2464\n\\]\n\nTo verify, we can use the standard multiplication method:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n   32 \\\\\n\\times 77 \\\\\n\\hline\n   224 \\quad (\\text{32} \\times 7) \\\\\n+2240 \\quad (\\text{32} \\times 70) \\\\\n\\hline\n  2464 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 32 and 77 is \\(\\boxed{2464}\\).",
