)(90 + 1). Applying FOIL:\n\nFirst: 70\u00d790 = 6300,\n\nOuter: 70\u00d71 =70,\n\nInner: 3\u00d790 =270,\n\nLast: 3\u00d71=3.\n\nAdding all these: 6300 +70 =6370, plus 270 =6640, plus 3 =6643. Same result.\n\nAlternatively, using another method: 73\u00d791 =73\u00d7(90+1)=73\u00d790 +73\u00d71.\n\n73\u00d790: 73\u00d79\u00d710. 73\u00d79 is 657, so 657\u00d710=6570. Then add 73 gives 6570 +73 =6643. Yep, that matches.\n\nHmm, so I think that's correct. Let me just cross-verify with another approach. Maybe breaking down 91 into 100 - 9.\n\nWait, 91 is 100 - 9, so 73\u00d791 =73\u00d7(100 -9)=73\u00d7100 -73\u00d79=7300 -657. Let's compute that. 7300 minus 657.\n\nSubtracting 600 from 7300 gives 6700, then subtract 57 more: 6700 -57 =6643. That works as well. So all methods give 6643. So I think that's the correct product.\n\nWait a second, but in my initial thought process, I confused the numbers with 08 and 65, but then corrected to 73 and 91. So the final answer here is 6643.\n\nLet me just do one more check using a calculator-like approach. 73 times 90 is 6570, plus 73 is 6643. Yep, that's consistent.\n\nAlternatively, multiplying step by step:\n\n       73\n     \u00d7 91\n     -------\nFirst, multiply 73 by 1: 73.\n\nThen multiply 73 by 9 (the tens digit, so actually 90), so 73\u00d79=657, shifted one position to the left becomes 6570.\n\nAdding 73 +6570:\n\n73 +6570. Let's add 6570 + 70 =6640, then +3 =6643. Correct.\n\nTherefore, the product of 73 and 91 is 6643.\n\nBut wait, hold on, let me make sure I didn't make any arithmetic errors. For instance, 73\u00d79:\n\n70\u00d79=630, 3\u00d79=27, so 630+27=657. That's correct.\n\nThen 657\u00d710=6570. Then 6570+73: 6570 +70 is 6640, plus 3 is 6643. All correct.\n\nAlternatively, if I think of 73\u00d791 as (70+3)(90+1), using the distributive property:\n\n70\u00d790 = 6300,\n\n70\u00d71 =70,\n\n3\u00d790=270,\n\n3\u00d71=3.\n\nAdding all together: 6300+70 is 6370, plus 270 is 6640, plus 3 is 6643. Yep.\n\nHmm, seems consistent across multiple methods. So I think that's the right answer. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations here. So, yeah, the product should be 6643.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 73 and 91 is \\boxed{6643}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 73 and 91, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm and verify using the distributive property.\n\nFirst, using the standard multiplication method:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n     73 \\\\\n   \\times 91 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     73 \\quad \\text{(73 multiplied by 1)} \\\\\n   +6570 \\quad \\text{(73 multiplied by 90, shifted one position to the left)} \\\\\n   \\hline\n     6643 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nBreaking down the multiplication step-by-step:\n1. Multiply 73 by 1 (units place of 91):\n   \\[\n   73 \\times 1 = 73\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 73 by 90 (tens place of 91, which is 9 in the tens place):\n   \\[\n   73 \\times 9 = 657 \\quad \\text{(then add a zero to account for the tens place)} \\quad \\Rightarrow 6570\n   \\]\n3. Add the results of the two partial products:\n   \\[\n   73 + 6570 = 6643\n   \\]\n\nVerification using the distributive property (FOIL method):\n\\[\n73 \\times 91 = (70 + 3)(90 + 1)\n\\]\nExpanding the terms:\n\\[\n= 70 \\times 90 + 70 \\times 1 + 3 \\times 90 + 3 \\times 1\n\\]\nCalculating each term:\n\\[\n70 \\times 90 = 6300 \\\\\n70 \\times 1 = 70 \\\\\n3 \\times 90 = 270 \\\\\n3 \\times 1 = 3\n\\]\nAdding all the terms together:\n\\[\n6300 + 70 + 270 + 3 = 6300 + 70 = 6370 \\\\\n6370 + 270 = 6640 \\\\\n6640 + 3 = 6643\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 73 and 91 is \\(\\boxed{6643}\\).",
