her:\n\n7200 + 360 = 7560,\n\nthen subtract (80 + 4) which is 84,\n\nso 7560 - 84 = 7476.\n\nOkay, that matches the standard algorithm result. So the correct answer is 7476. Therefore, my initial mistake was probably in the first method's breakdown where I incorrectly split the numbers. It's important to split them correctly to apply the distributive property accurately. So the product of 89 and 84 is 7476.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 89 and 84 is \\boxed{7476}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 89 and 84, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. Multiply 89 by 4:\n   \\[\n   89 \\times 4 = 356\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 89 by 80 (since the 8 is in the tens place):\n   \\[\n   89 \\times 80 = 7120\n   \\]\n3. Add the results of the two multiplications:\n   \\[\n   356 + 7120 = 7476\n   \\]\n\nWe can also verify this using the distributive property by expressing 89 as \\(90 - 1\\) and 84 as \\(80 + 4\\):\n\\[\n(90 - 1)(80 + 4) = 90 \\times 80 + 90 \\times 4 - 1 \\times 80 - 1 \\times 4\n\\]\nCalculating each term:\n\\[\n90 \\times 80 = 7200\n\\]\n\\[\n90 \\times 4 = 360\n\\]\n\\[\n1 \\times 80 = 80\n\\]\n\\[\n1 \\times 4 = 4\n\\]\nCombining these terms:\n\\[\n7200 + 360 - 80 - 4 = 7200 + 360 = 7560\n\\]\n\\[\n7560 - 84 = 7476\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 89 and 84 is \\(\\boxed{7476}\\).",
