nfidently say the product of 26 and 37 is 962.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 26 and 37 is \\boxed{962}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 26 and 37, we can use the standard multiplication method:\n\n1. **Multiply 26 by 7 (the ones place of 37):**\n   - \\(6 \\times 7 = 42\\), write down 2 and carry over 4.\n   - \\(2 \\times 7 = 14\\), add the carried over 4 to get 18.\n   - The first partial product is 182.\n\n2. **Multiply 26 by 3 (the tens place of 37, which is actually 30):**\n   - \\(6 \\times 3 = 18\\), write down 8 and carry over 1.\n   - \\(2 \\times 3 = 6\\), add the carried over 1 to get 7.\n   - Since this is the tens place, shift one position to the left, resulting in 780.\n\n3. **Add the partial products:**\n   - \\(182 + 780 = 962\\).\n\nTo verify, we can use the distributive property:\n- \\(26 \\times 37 = 26 \\times (30 + 7) = (26 \\times 30) + (26 \\times 7)\\)\n- \\(26 \\times 30 = 780\\)\n- \\(26 \\times 7 = 182\\)\n- Adding these gives \\(780 + 182 = 962\\).\n\nAnother verification using division:\n- \\(962 \\div 26 = 37\\)\n- \\(962 \\div 37 = 26\\)\n\nBoth verifications confirm the result is correct.\n\nThe product of 26 and 37 is \\(\\boxed{962}\\).",
