same result.\n\nAlright, so I think 2773 is the correct product of 59 and 47. The first time I did the vertical method, I probably made an arithmetic mistake in the intermediate steps, but after redoing it carefully and cross-checking with other methods like distributive property and breaking into easier numbers, it's consistent. So I'm confident the answer is 2773.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 59 and 47 is calculated as follows:\n\n1. **Break down using distributive property:**\n   \\[\n   59 \\times 47 = (50 + 9) \\times (40 + 7)\n   \\]\n   Expand the terms:\n   \\[\n   = (50 \\times 40) + (50 \\times 7) + (9 \\times 40) + (9 \\times 7)\n   \\]\n   Calculate each part:\n   \\[\n   = 2000 + 350 + 360 + 63 = 2773\n   \\]\n\n2. **Verification via vertical multiplication:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     \\phantom{0}59 \\\\\n   \\times 47 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     \\phantom{0}413 \\quad (\\text{59 \u00d7 7}) \\\\\n   +2360 \\quad (\\text{59 \u00d7 40}) \\\\\n   \\hline\n     2773 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Alternative method (adjusting numbers):**\n   \\[\n   59 \\times 47 = 59 \\times (50 - 3) = (59 \\times 50) - (59 \\times 3) = 2950 - 177 = 2773\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**  \n\\boxed{2773}",
