 = (50+8)x36 =50x36 +8x36.\n\n50x36: 50x30=1500, 50x6=300, so total 1800.\n\n8x36: 8x30=240, 8x6=48. 240+48=288.\n\nAdding 1800+288=2088. Yep, same result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe do 36x60=2160, then subtract 36x2=72, so 2160-72=2088. That also works. So that's another way to compute mentally. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 2088. My initial mistake was probably due to miscalculating in the first method when I confused the numbers. But after rechecking with different methods, it's consistent. So I think the correct product is 2088.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 58 and 36 is calculated as follows:\n\n1. **Multiply 58 by 6 (ones place of 36):**\n   \\[\n   58 \\times 6 = 348\n   \\]\n2. **Multiply 58 by 30 (tens place of 36):**\n   \\[\n   58 \\times 30 = 1,\\!740\n   \\]\n3. **Add the results from steps 1 and 2:**\n   \\[\n   348 + 1,\\!740 = 2,\\!088\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:** \\boxed{2088}",
