f 79 and 55 is 4345.\n\nI think that's solid. The confusion earlier was because I started with different numbers, but after correcting myself, all methods lead to 4345. So I can confidently say that's the answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 79 and 55 is \\boxed{4345}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 79 and 55, we can use the distributive property by breaking down 55 into 50 and 5:\n\n\\[\n79 \\times 55 = 79 \\times (50 + 5)\n\\]\n\nFirst, calculate \\(79 \\times 50\\):\n\\[\n79 \\times 50 = 3950\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate \\(79 \\times 5\\):\n\\[\n79 \\times 5 = 395\n\\]\n\nAdd the two results together:\n\\[\n3950 + 395 = 4345\n\\]\n\nWe can verify this using another method by expanding \\((80 - 1)(50 + 5)\\):\n\\[\n(80 - 1)(50 + 5) = 80 \\times 50 + 80 \\times 5 - 1 \\times 50 - 1 \\times 5\n\\]\n\\[\n= 4000 + 400 - 50 - 5\n\\]\n\\[\n= 4000 + 400 = 4400\n\\]\n\\[\n4400 - 50 = 4350\n\\]\n\\[\n4350 - 5 = 4345\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product is indeed \\(\\boxed{4345}\\).",
