. Shift the result one place to the left:\n   \\[\n   54 \\times 30 = 1620\n   \\]\n   Partial product: 1620\n\n4. Add the two partial products:\n   \\[\n   270 + 1620 = 1890\n   \\]\n\nWe can verify this using the distributive property:\n\\[\n35 \\times 54 = (30 + 5)(50 + 4) = 30 \\times 50 + 30 \\times 4 + 5 \\times 50 + 5 \\times 4\n\\]\n\\[\n= 1500 + 120 + 250 + 20 = 1500 + 120 = 1620; \\quad 1620 + 250 = 1870; \\quad 1870 + 20 = 1890\n\\]\n\nAnother verification:\n\\[\n35 \\times 54 = 35 \\times (50 + 4) = 35 \\times 50 + 35 \\times 4 = 1750 + 140 = 1890\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 35 and 54 is \\boxed{1890}.",
