\n46 x 85.\n\nFirst, 46 multiplied by 5 (units place):\n\n5*6 = 30, write 0, carryover 3.\n\n5*4 =20 +3 =23. So first partial product is 230.\n\nThen, 46 multiplied by 8 (tens place, so actually 80):\n\n8*6 =48, write 8, carryover 4.\n\n8*4 =32 +4 =36. So that partial product is 368, but since it's the tens place, we shift one position to the left, making it 3680.\n\nAdding 230 + 3680:\n\n230 + 3680:\n\n230 + 3680:\n\n3680 + 200 = 3880,\n\n3880 + 30 = 3910. Yep, same result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe converting to hundreds or something? 46*85. Let's think of 85 as 100 -15.\n\nSo 46*(100 -15) = 4600 - (46*15).\n\nCalculate 46*15: 46*10=460, 46*5=230, so total 460+230=690.\n\nThus, 4600 - 690 = 3910. Same answer again.\n\nHmm, so all methods give me 3910, so that must be the correct product. I just need to make sure I didn't make any arithmetic errors in my steps. Let me check each term again in the distributive method:\n\n40x80 is indeed 3200,\n\n40x5 is 200,\n\n6x80 is 480,\n\n6x5 is 30. Adding them: 3200+200 is 3400,\n\n3400+480 is 3880,\n\n3880+30=3910. Perfect.\n\nAlternatively, using calculator-like approach: 46 multiplied by 85. Let me do 45*85 first, which is (40*85)+(5*85)= 3400 +425=3825. Then add 1*85 to get 3825 +85= 3910. Yep.\n\nOkay, so after multiple methods and checks, I'm confident the answer is 3910. The initial confusion was because I started thinking about a different problem (32 and 19), but corrected myself. So the correct product of 46 and 85 is 3910.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 46 and 85 is \\boxed{3910}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 46 and 85, we can use the distributive property and standard multiplication algorithm.\n\nFirst, using the distributive property:\n\\[\n46 \\times 85 = (40 + 6) \\times (80 + 5)\n\\]\nExpanding this, we get:\n\\[\n40 \\times 80 + 40 \\times 5 + 6 \\times 80 + 6 \\times 5\n\\]\nCalculating each term:\n\\[\n40 \\times 80 = 3200\n\\]\n\\[\n40 \\times 5 = 200\n\\]\n\\[\n6 \\times 80 = 480\n\\]\n\\[\n6 \\times 5 = 30\n\\]\nAdding these results together:\n\\[\n3200 + 200 + 480 + 30 = 3200 + 200 = 3400\n\\]\n\\[\n3400 + 480 = 3880\n\\]\n\\[\n3880 + 30 = 3910\n\\]\n\nUsing the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n   46 \\\\\n\\times 85 \\\\\n\\hline\n   230 & \\text{(46 multiplied by 5)} \\\\\n+3680 & \\text{(46 multiplied by 80, shifted one position to the left)} \\\\\n\\hline\n  3910 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 46 and 85 is \\(\\boxed{3910}\\).",
